//! tree — the writable file tree, in memory (px27).
//!
//! Written from man-pages `open(2)`, `write(2)`, `truncate(2)`,
//! `mkdir(2)`, `rmdir(2)`, `unlink(2)`, `rename(2)`, `stat(2)`,
//! `getdents64(2)`, `inode(7)`, `path_resolution(7)` and `tmpfs(5)`,
//! POSIX.1-2024, and black-box runs on Linux's tmpfs: strace of
//! boreutils' file changers, pelt and lobo (`notes/px27/straces/`) and a
//! static C probe that prints what Linux answers (user/elf/tree.c). No
//! Linux source; no other kernel's or file system's source.
//!
//! **Inodes.** A file or a directory is an inode: 16 words (128 bytes)
//! in a table that grows a frame at a time, 32 to a frame, at most
//! 16,384 (the table's one root frame holds 512 pointers). An inode is
//! named by its index; kernel/files keeps the descriptors and the
//! paths and asks here. Its words: the mode (0: a free record), the
//! link count, the size, the holders (open files, working
//! directories, and a removed directory's hold on its parent), the
//! three times and the time it was made (nanoseconds since the epoch),
//! where its bytes are, and for a directory its parent and how many
//! entries it has, and (px42) its owner and its group. A freed inode
//! goes on a list and is the next one made; the table's frames are
//! never given back (at most 512).
//!
//! **Owners (px42).** An inode's last word holds its owner's user id
//! (the low 32 bits) and its group's id (the high 32). The sixteen
//! words were all named before, but one of them, the free list's link,
//! was only ever used by a record that is free: the link now lives in
//! the word a live inode keeps its birth time in, and the inode is the
//! 128 bytes it was. `create`, `mkdir`, `symlink` and `mksock` are told
//! the ids to stamp (kernel/files reads them from the maker's
//! file-system ids and the directory, `stamp`); `chown` changes them;
//! `adopt` takes the archive's. The tree asks nobody who they are: who
//! may change an owner is kernel/files' rule.
//!
//! **A file's bytes** are 4096-byte frames under an index whose depth
//! grows with the file: depth 0, the one frame alone (up to 4096
//! bytes); depth 1, a frame of 512 pointers (2 MiB); depth 2, a frame
//! of pointers to those (1 GiB, the largest file: a write past it is
//! -EFBIG). A page never written has no frame and reads as zeros (the
//! page of zeros made with the tree), as tmpfs keeps a hole.
//! `cut` gives back every frame past a new size, an index frame with
//! its last pointer, and zeroes the tail of the page that stays.
//!
//! **The initramfs under it.** `start` makes an inode for every
//! archive entry: a directory a directory, a file an inode whose bytes
//! are the archive's own, in place (`I_BACK`, `I_BACKLEN`), with no
//! frame. A read comes from the archive where no frame has been
//! written; the first write to a page copies that page into a frame; a
//! truncation cuts how much of the archive the file still reads. The
//! archive's pages are Limine's module and are never given back. A
//! symbolic link of the archive (px64: cpio(5)'s mode 0120000, its data
//! the target; `/bin/grep -> scent`) is made a link of the tree, as
//! `symlink(2)` makes one, its target copied into a frame, owned and
//! timed as the archive says. A device or a FIFO of the archive is
//! still left out.
//!
//! **A directory** is a file of records, none across a page: the
//! inode's index + 1 (0: a free record) in 4 bytes, the record's
//! length and the name's in 2 each, the name. A new page is one free
//! record; a name takes the first free record it fits and leaves the
//! rest free; a removed name's record is free again and joins the free
//! records after it. Records never move, so a position in a directory
//! (a record's offset) stays good while the directory changes:
//! `entry_at` answers the first live record at or after it, found from
//! the page's start. A directory with no entry holds no frame.
//!
//! **The cap.** The tree holds at most half of the frames that were
//! free when it was made (tmpfs's default is half of memory), and
//! takes none when fewer than RESERVE would be left free: `grab`
//! answers 0 and the caller answers -ENOSPC. Every frame it holds is
//! counted (`held`), every inode (`live`).
//!
//! **Times** come from the wall clock kernel/user set at boot
//! (boot/user.S's word 6) plus the ticks since: 10 ms steps.
//!
//! **Links and changes (px36).** A file may have many names (`link`:
//! a second record leading to the same inode; the inode and its bytes
//! go when the last name and the last holder are gone). A symbolic link
//! is an inode of its own, S_IFLNK|0777, whose bytes are its target,
//! held as a file's; kernel/files follows it. `set_mode`, `set_times`
//! (signed nanoseconds, to the nanosecond) and `chown` (px36's `owned`,
//! root to root; px42: any id) are the changes after a file is made;
//! each moves ctime. Written
//! from `link(2)`, `symlink(2)`, `symlink(7)`, `chmod(2)`, `chown(2)`,
//! `utimensat(2)` and black-box runs on tmpfs (`notes/px36/`).
//!
//! **FIFOs, shared memory and the page cache (px62).** A FIFO is an
//! inode of its own (`mkfifo`) holding no bytes: kernel/files' pipe
//! buffer carries what is written, and the FIFO keeps which buffer and
//! how many times each end has been opened. Shared memory that is no
//! file's is an inode with no name (`anon`), held by its mappings. A
//! file's frames are the only copy of its bytes, so they are what a
//! mapping maps (`page`, kernel/vm): a mapping of a page still the
//! archive's gives that page its frame then, as a first write does.
//! Written from `fifo(7)`, `mknod(2)`, `mmap(2)` and `tmpfs(5)`.
//!
//! **Two stores (px63).** A record may stand for an inode of an ext2
//! volume instead (kernel/ext2, on a disk of kernel/block's): the tree's
//! operations are one interface over both. Such a record keeps only what
//! is the memory's — its holders, a directory's parent record (held),
//! a running count, a FIFO's words, the frames a mapping of it has filled
//! (px62's page cache, reused: `page`) — and its mode and link count
//! mirrored; its size, times, owner, blocks, bytes and directory entries
//! are the volume's, asked for every time. A side table beside the
//! inode table says which records are a volume's (the ext2 number, the
//! volume) and chains them in a hash by number, so an inode in use has
//! one record. A record nobody holds is kept while there are fewer than
//! VOL_KEEP of them, then the oldest not looked up in the current system
//! call are given back (`evict`); an inode with no name left goes off the
//! disk with its last holder. A volume is mounted on a directory of the
//! memory (`mount`): a lookup that finds that directory answers the
//! volume's root, whose parent is the directory's parent, so `..`,
//! `getcwd` and a path through it are as on Linux; the covered directory
//! cannot be removed or renamed (-EBUSY), and a rename or a link between
//! stores is -EXDEV. Written from `mount(2)`, `rename(2)`, `link(2)` and
//! `path_resolution(7)`.
//!
//! One CPU, and a system call runs with interrupts off from entry to
//! return, so nothing here locks: a `rename` is every check, then the
//! room for the new name, then the change, with no call between. No
//! region, no heap.

use ext2
use frames
use initramfs
use paging
use panic
use timer

extern "c" fn pax_tree_copy(dst: u64, src: u64, n: u64)
extern "c" fn pax_tree_zero(dst: u64, n: u64)
extern "c" let pax_tree_state: *u64
extern "c" let pax_syscall_state: *u64

const PAGE: u64 = 4096
const PTRS: u64 = 512
const IWORDS: u64 = 16
const IPF: u64 = 32 // inodes a frame
/// The most inodes there can be.
pub const MAX_INODES: u64 = 16384
/// Frames the tree never takes the machine below.
pub const RESERVE: u64 = 2048
/// The longest name (`NAME_MAX`).
pub const NAME_MAX: u64 = 255
/// The largest file: what two levels of index hold.
pub const MAX_SIZE: u64 = 0x40000000
/// No inode.
pub const NONE: u64 = 0xffffffff
const NS_PER_SEC: u64 = 1000000000
const NS_PER_TICK: u64 = 10000151 // kernel/user's

// pax_tree_state's words.
const S_READY: u64 = 0
const S_TABLE: u64 = 1 // the inode table's root frame
const S_LIVE: u64 = 2 // inodes in use
const S_HELD: u64 = 3 // frames held
const S_CAP: u64 = 4 // the most it may hold
const S_FREE: u64 = 5 // the free inodes' list: an index + 1, 0 none
const S_NEXT: u64 = 6 // the first index never used
const S_REFUSED: u64 = 7 // refusals by name, counted
const S_ZERO: u64 = 8 // the page of zeros
const S_STAMP: u64 = 9 // while the tree is made: the time every change is stamped with, + 1
const S_BASE: u64 = 10 // frames held once the archive is in
const S_BASE_LIVE: u64 = 11 // and inodes
const S_UNLINKS: u64 = 12 // names of files removed since boot
const S_CENSUS: u64 = 13 // the count the last census line was for
const S_FULL: u64 = 14 // 0: there is room; 1: a frame was refused, not yet said; 2: said
const S_ITABLE: u64 = 15 // frames of inodes (never given back)
const S_BASE_ITABLE: u64 = 16 // and when the archive was in
const S_VOLF: u64 = 17 // px63: the volumes' frame (physical): the mounts, the side table's frames, the hash; 0 before the first mount
const S_GEN: u64 = 18 // px63: system calls since boot (`tick`): a volume record's stamp
const S_VLIVE: u64 = 19 // px63: records standing for a volume's inodes (not in S_LIVE)
const S_VEVICT: u64 = 20 // px63: of them, given back while their inode lives
const S_VSIDE: u64 = 21 // px63: frames of the side table and the hash
const S_ROOTM: u64 = 22 // px67: the root mount + 1 (`/` on a volume, kernel/fstab's `root=`); 0: `/` is the memory's ROOT

// An inode's words.
const I_MODE: u64 = 0
const I_NLINK: u64 = 1
const I_SIZE: u64 = 2
const I_REFS: u64 = 3
const I_ATIME: u64 = 4
const I_MTIME: u64 = 5
const I_CTIME: u64 = 6
const I_ROOT: u64 = 7 // the index's root frame (depth 0: the data frame); 0 none
const I_DEPTH: u64 = 8
const I_BLOCKS: u64 = 9 // data frames held
const I_BACK: u64 = 10 // the archive's bytes (a kernel address); 0 none
const I_BACKLEN: u64 = 11 // how many of them the file still reads
const I_PARENT: u64 = 12 // a directory's parent; px34: a socket's record (kernel/unix), + 1, while it lives
const I_RUNNING: u64 = 12 // px56: a regular file's: how many programs run from it (the word no file used)
const I_ENTRIES: u64 = 13 // a directory's entries; a file: its archive entry + 1
const I_BTIME: u64 = 14
const I_NEXT: u64 = 14 // the free list: a free record's link, in the word a live inode's birth time is in (px42)
const I_OWNER: u64 = 15 // px42: the owner's user id (low 32 bits) and the group's id (high 32)
/// px42: the id `chown` leaves alone (-1 as 32 bits).
pub const KEEP: u64 = 0xffffffff

const S_IFMT: u64 = 0xf000
const S_IFDIR: u64 = 0x4000
const S_IFREG: u64 = 0x8000
const S_IFSOCK: u64 = 0xc000 // px34
const S_IFLNK: u64 = 0xa000 // px36
const S_IFIFO: u64 = 0x1000 // px62
const S_ISUID: u64 = 0x800 // px36
const S_ISGID: u64 = 0x400
const S_IXGRP: u64 = 0x8
/// px36: a symbolic link's target at least this long costs a page in
/// `st_blocks`; a shorter one costs none (tmpfs keeps it with the
/// inode: measured, `symlink: blocks by the target's length`).
const LINK_INLINE: u64 = 128

// errnos (uapi asm-generic/errno-base.h, errno.h)
const ENOENT: u64 = 2
const ENOTDIR: u64 = 20
const EISDIR: u64 = 21
const EINVAL: u64 = 22
const EFBIG: u64 = 27
const ENOSPC: u64 = 28
const ENOTEMPTY: u64 = 39
const EIO: u64 = 5 // px63, with the next five
const EXDEV: u64 = 18
const EBUSY: u64 = 16
const EROFS: u64 = 30
const ENOMEM: u64 = 12
const EMLINK: u64 = 31

fn neg(e: u64) -> u64 {
    0xffffffffffffffff - e + 1
}

/// Whether `r` is an -errno.
pub fn failed(r: u64) -> bool {
    r >= 0xfffffffffffff001
}

fn rd(a: u64) -> u64 {
    // # Safety: `a` is a word of the tree's state or of a frame the tree
    // holds, through the HHDM, 8-aligned.
    unsafe { (a as *u64).read_volatile() }
}

fn wr(a: u64, v: u64) {
    // # Safety: as `rd`.
    unsafe { (a as *u64).write_volatile(v) }
}

fn rd8(a: u64) -> u64 {
    // # Safety: a byte of a frame the tree holds, of the archive, or of
    // the caller's kernel buffer.
    let v = unsafe { (a as *u8).read_volatile() }
    v as u64
}

fn rd16(a: u64) -> u64 {
    // # Safety: a directory record's field, 2-aligned, in a frame the
    // tree holds.
    let v = unsafe { (a as *u16).read_volatile() }
    v as u64
}

fn wr16(a: u64, v: u64) {
    // # Safety: as `rd16`.
    unsafe { (a as *u16).write_volatile((v & 0xffff) as u16) }
}

fn rd32(a: u64) -> u64 {
    // # Safety: as `rd16`, 4-aligned.
    let v = unsafe { (a as *u32).read_volatile() }
    v as u64
}

fn wr32(a: u64, v: u64) {
    // # Safety: as `rd32`.
    unsafe { (a as *u32).write_volatile((v & 0xffffffff) as u32) }
}

fn st(i: u64) -> u64 {
    // # Safety: i < 32, inside boot/tree.S's pax_tree_state.
    unsafe { ((pax_tree_state as u64 + i * 8) as *u64).read_volatile() }
}

fn put_st(i: u64, v: u64) {
    // # Safety: as `st`.
    unsafe { ((pax_tree_state as u64 + i * 8) as *u64).write_volatile(v) }
}

fn hh() -> u64 {
    frames.hhdm()
}

fn bcopy(dst: u64, src: u64, n: u64) {
    // # Safety: [dst, dst + n) is inside one frame (the tree's, or a
    // user page the caller checked, through the HHDM) and [src, src + n)
    // inside a frame, the archive or the caller's kernel buffer; the
    // two do not overlap.
    unsafe { pax_tree_copy(dst, src, n) }
}

fn zero(dst: u64, n: u64) {
    // # Safety: [dst, dst + n) is inside one frame, through the HHDM.
    unsafe { pax_tree_zero(dst, n) }
}

/// Nanoseconds since the epoch (kernel/user's wall clock: the CMOS
/// clock's reading at boot plus the ticks since); while the tree is
/// made, the archive entry's own time.
fn now() -> u64 {
    let s = st(S_STAMP)
    if s != 0 {
        return s - 1
    }
    // # Safety: word 6 of the 64-byte pax_syscall_state (kernel/user's
    // U_EPOCH).
    let epoch = unsafe { ((pax_syscall_state as u64 + 48) as *u64).read_volatile() }
    epoch * NS_PER_SEC + timer.ticks() * NS_PER_TICK
}

// --- frames --------------------------------------------------------------------

/// One more frame for the tree, zeroed: its physical address, or 0 at
/// the cap or when the machine would be left with fewer than RESERVE.
fn grab() -> u64 {
    if st(S_HELD) >= st(S_CAP) || frames.free_count() <= RESERVE {
        if st(S_FULL) == 0 {
            put_st(S_FULL, 1)
        }
        return 0
    }
    let pa = frames.alloc() else 0
    if pa == 0 {
        return 0
    }
    zero(pa + hh(), PAGE)
    put_st(S_HELD, st(S_HELD) + 1)
    pa
}

fn give(pa: u64) {
    frames.free(pa)
    put_st(S_HELD, st(S_HELD) - 1)
    put_st(S_FULL, 0)
}

/// Whether the tree has just refused a frame for the first time since
/// it last gave one back (kernel/user says so once, by name).
pub fn full_news() -> bool {
    if st(S_FULL) != 1 {
        return false
    }
    put_st(S_FULL, 2)
    true
}

/// The count of files' names removed since boot when it has just
/// reached a multiple of 2500 (kernel/user's census line), else 0.
pub fn census_due() -> u64 {
    let n = st(S_UNLINKS)
    if n == 0 || n % 2500 != 0 || st(S_CENSUS) == n {
        return 0
    }
    put_st(S_CENSUS, n)
    n
}

/// Frames the tree holds.
pub fn held() -> u64 {
    st(S_HELD)
}

/// The most it may hold.
pub fn cap() -> u64 {
    st(S_CAP)
}

/// Inodes in use.
pub fn live() -> u64 {
    st(S_LIVE)
}

/// Frames (0) and inodes (1) it held once the archive was in (`start`),
/// and how many of those frames were the inode table's (2).
pub fn base(which: int) -> u64 {
    if which == 0 {
        return st(S_BASE)
    }
    if which == 2 {
        return st(S_BASE_ITABLE)
    }
    st(S_BASE_LIVE)
}

/// Frames of the inode table: they grow with the most inodes there
/// have been at once and are never given back (at most 512).
pub fn table_frames() -> u64 {
    st(S_ITABLE)
}

/// A call or a flag refused by name: counted.
pub fn refuse() {
    put_st(S_REFUSED, st(S_REFUSED) + 1)
}

/// How many were.
pub fn refusals() -> u64 {
    st(S_REFUSED)
}

// --- inodes --------------------------------------------------------------------

fn iaddr(i: u64) -> u64 {
    let f = rd(st(S_TABLE) + hh() + (i / IPF) * 8)
    f + hh() + (i % IPF) * IWORDS * 8
}

fn ig(i: u64, w: u64) -> u64 {
    rd(iaddr(i) + w * 8)
}

fn ip(i: u64, w: u64, v: u64) {
    wr(iaddr(i) + w * 8, v)
}

/// A new inode with `mode`, owned `uid`:`gid` (px42), no link yet,
/// every time now: its index, or NONE (the table full, or no frame for
/// it).
fn inode_new(mode: u64, uid: u64, gid: u64) -> u64 {
    var i = NONE
    let head = st(S_FREE)
    if head != 0 {
        i = head - 1
        put_st(S_FREE, ig(i, I_NEXT))
    } else {
        i = st(S_NEXT)
        if i >= MAX_INODES {
            return NONE
        }
        if i % IPF == 0 {
            let pa = grab()
            if pa == 0 {
                return NONE
            }
            wr(st(S_TABLE) + hh() + (i / IPF) * 8, pa)
            put_st(S_ITABLE, st(S_ITABLE) + 1)
        }
        put_st(S_NEXT, i + 1)
    }
    var w: u64 = 0
    while w < IWORDS {
        ip(i, w, 0)
        w += 1
    }
    put_side(i, 0)
    let t = now()
    ip(i, I_MODE, mode)
    ip(i, I_ATIME, t)
    ip(i, I_MTIME, t)
    ip(i, I_CTIME, t)
    ip(i, I_BTIME, t)
    ip(i, I_OWNER, pack(uid, gid))
    put_st(S_LIVE, st(S_LIVE) + 1)
    i
}

fn pack(uid: u64, gid: u64) -> u64 {
    (uid & 0xffffffff) | ((gid & 0xffffffff) << 32)
}

/// px63: inode `i`'s owner and group, from whichever store it is in.
fn owner_of(i: u64) -> (u64, u64) {
    if on_volume(i) {
        return ext2.owner(vol(i), vino(i))
    }
    (ig(i, I_OWNER) & 0xffffffff, ig(i, I_OWNER) >> 32)
}

/// px42: inode `i`'s owner, a user id.
pub fn uid(i: u64) -> u64 {
    if on_volume(i) {
        let (u, _g) = ext2.owner(vol(i), vino(i))
        return u
    }
    ig(i, I_OWNER) & 0xffffffff
}

/// px42: inode `i`'s group, a group id.
pub fn gid(i: u64) -> u64 {
    if on_volume(i) {
        let (_u, g) = ext2.owner(vol(i), vino(i))
        return g
    }
    ig(i, I_OWNER) >> 32
}

/// Inode `i` is gone for good: its bytes given back, its record free.
fn inode_free(i: u64) {
    cut(i, 0)
    let dir = ig(i, I_MODE) & S_IFMT == S_IFDIR
    let p = ig(i, I_PARENT)
    ip(i, I_MODE, 0)
    ip(i, I_NEXT, st(S_FREE))
    put_st(S_FREE, i + 1)
    put_st(S_LIVE, st(S_LIVE) - 1)
    if dir && p != i {
        release(p) // a removed directory held its parent (`..` still led there)
    }
}

/// One more holder of inode `i` (an open file, a working directory).
pub fn hold(i: u64) {
    ip(i, I_REFS, ig(i, I_REFS) + 1)
}

/// One holder fewer; the last one of an inode with no name left frees
/// it, and its frames go back.
pub fn release(i: u64) {
    let r = ig(i, I_REFS)
    if r > 0 {
        ip(i, I_REFS, r - 1)
    }
    if r <= 1 && ig(i, I_NLINK) == 0 {
        if on_volume(i) {
            vgone(i) // px63: off the disk with its last holder
        } else {
            inode_free(i)
        }
    }
}

/// Inode `i`'s mode (type and permission bits).
pub fn mode(i: u64) -> u64 {
    ig(i, I_MODE)
}

/// Whether inode `i` is a directory.
pub fn is_dir(i: u64) -> bool {
    ig(i, I_MODE) & S_IFMT == S_IFDIR
}

/// Its link count: 0 once its last name is gone.
pub fn nlink(i: u64) -> u64 {
    ig(i, I_NLINK)
}

/// Its size as `stat` answers it: a file's bytes; a directory's 40 and
/// 20 an entry, tmpfs's numbers (measured), which `ls -l` prints.
pub fn size(i: u64) -> u64 {
    if on_volume(i) {
        return ext2.size(vol(i), vino(i)) // px63: the volume's (a directory's whole blocks)
    }
    if is_dir(i) {
        if ig(i, I_NLINK) == 0 {
            return 40
        }
        return 40 + 20 * ig(i, I_ENTRIES)
    }
    ig(i, I_SIZE)
}

/// A directory's parent (the root's is the root).
pub fn parent(i: u64) -> u64 {
    let m = root_of(i)
    if m != MOUNTS {
        // px63: a mount's root: the covered directory's parent; px67: the
        // root mount's root is `/`, whose parent is itself, never the
        // memory's ROOT it covers (tests/mpx6-root's `cd /..`).
        if st(S_ROOTM) == m + 1 {
            return i
        }
        return parent(mw(m, M_POINT) - 1)
    }
    ig(i, I_PARENT)
}

/// Inode `i`'s time `which`: 0 atime, 1 mtime, 2 ctime, 3 when it was
/// made; nanoseconds since the epoch.
pub fn time(i: u64, which: int) -> u64 {
    if on_volume(i) {
        return ext2.time(vol(i), vino(i), which)
    }
    if which == 0 {
        return ig(i, I_ATIME)
    }
    if which == 1 {
        return ig(i, I_MTIME)
    }
    if which == 2 {
        return ig(i, I_CTIME)
    }
    ig(i, I_BTIME)
}

/// px56: whether inode `i` is a regular file (what `execve` loads).
pub fn is_regular(i: u64) -> bool {
    ig(i, I_MODE) & S_IFMT == S_IFREG
}

/// px56 (pax#95): how many programs run from regular file `i` (each
/// process's program is an open file of kernel/files', which counts
/// itself here when it is made and when it goes): while any does,
/// kernel/files refuses to open the file for writing, -ETXTBSY
/// (`open(2)`, measured). The word is a directory's parent's and a
/// socket's record's; a regular file never used it (0 from `create`
/// and `adopt`).
pub fn running(i: u64) -> u64 {
    if !is_regular(i) {
        return 0
    }
    ig(i, I_RUNNING)
}

pub fn run_hold(i: u64) {
    if is_regular(i) {
        ip(i, I_RUNNING, ig(i, I_RUNNING) + 1)
    }
}

pub fn run_release(i: u64) {
    if is_regular(i) && ig(i, I_RUNNING) > 0 {
        ip(i, I_RUNNING, ig(i, I_RUNNING) - 1)
    }
}

/// A file's 512-byte blocks: eight for every page that holds bytes, a
/// frame of the tree's or a page of the archive not yet written over.
/// px36: a symbolic link's are tmpfs's: none for a target shorter than
/// LINK_INLINE, eight for a longer one (its one frame).
pub fn blocks(i: u64) -> u64 {
    if on_volume(i) {
        return ext2.blocks512(vol(i), vino(i)) // px63: i_blocks, indirect blocks counted
    }
    if is_dir(i) {
        return 0
    }
    if is_link(i) {
        return if ig(i, I_SIZE) < LINK_INLINE { 0 } else { 8 }
    }
    let bl = ig(i, I_BACKLEN)
    var n = ig(i, I_BLOCKS)
    if bl != 0 {
        let pages = (bl + PAGE - 1) / PAGE
        if n == 0 {
            return pages * 8
        }
        var pg: u64 = 0
        while pg < pages {
            if frame_of(i, pg) == 0 {
                n += 1
            }
            pg += 1
        }
    }
    n * 8
}

/// Whether time `a` is not after time `b`: px36, times are signed
/// nanoseconds (a time set before 1970 is negative) held in a u64.
fn not_after(a: u64, b: u64) -> bool {
    (a ^ 0x8000000000000000) <= (b ^ 0x8000000000000000)
}

/// The read of a file sets its access time when that is not after its
/// last change (relatime's rule); px36: a symbolic link's too, when a
/// walk follows it or `readlink` reads it (measured on tmpfs).
pub fn touch_read(i: u64) {
    if on_volume(i) {
        let v = vol(i)
        let n = vino(i)
        if ext2.read_only(v) == 0 && (not_after(ext2.time(v, n, 0), ext2.time(v, n, 1)) || not_after(ext2.time(v, n, 0), ext2.time(v, n, 2))) {
            ext2.touch(v, n, ext2.T_ATIME, now())
        }
        return
    }
    if not_after(ig(i, I_ATIME), ig(i, I_MTIME)) || not_after(ig(i, I_ATIME), ig(i, I_CTIME)) {
        ip(i, I_ATIME, now())
    }
}

fn touch_change(i: u64) {
    if on_volume(i) {
        if ext2.read_only(vol(i)) == 0 {
            ext2.touch(vol(i), vino(i), ext2.T_MTIME | ext2.T_CTIME, now())
        }
        return
    }
    let t = now()
    ip(i, I_MTIME, t)
    ip(i, I_CTIME, t)
}

// --- a file's bytes --------------------------------------------------------------

fn cap_pages(d: u64) -> u64 {
    if d == 0 {
        return 1
    }
    if d == 1 {
        return PTRS
    }
    PTRS * PTRS
}

/// The frame holding page `pg` of inode `i`, or 0 (a hole, or a page
/// still the archive's).
fn frame_of(i: u64, pg: u64) -> u64 {
    let d = ig(i, I_DEPTH)
    let root = ig(i, I_ROOT)
    if root == 0 || pg >= cap_pages(d) {
        return 0
    }
    if d == 0 {
        return root
    }
    if d == 1 {
        return rd(root + hh() + pg * 8)
    }
    let mid = rd(root + hh() + (pg / PTRS) * 8)
    if mid == 0 {
        return 0
    }
    rd(mid + hh() + (pg % PTRS) * 8)
}

/// A new data frame for page `pg` of inode `i`: zeros, or the archive's
/// bytes for that page. 0 at the cap.
fn data_frame(i: u64, pg: u64) -> u64 {
    let pa = grab()
    if pa == 0 {
        return 0
    }
    if on_volume(i) {
        vfill(i, pg, pa + hh()) // px63: the page's bytes from the disk
    } else {
        let bl = ig(i, I_BACKLEN)
        if pg * PAGE < bl {
            let n = if bl - pg * PAGE < PAGE { bl - pg * PAGE } else { PAGE }
            bcopy(pa + hh(), ig(i, I_BACK) + pg * PAGE, n)
        }
    }
    ip(i, I_BLOCKS, ig(i, I_BLOCKS) + 1)
    pa
}

/// The frame holding page `pg` of inode `i`, made when there is none
/// (the index grown as far as it must be). 0 at the cap; the caller has
/// refused a page past the largest file.
fn frame_for(i: u64, pg: u64) -> u64 {
    while pg >= cap_pages(ig(i, I_DEPTH)) {
        let d = ig(i, I_DEPTH)
        if d >= 2 {
            return 0
        }
        let root = ig(i, I_ROOT)
        if root != 0 {
            let n = grab()
            if n == 0 {
                return 0
            }
            wr(n + hh(), root)
            ip(i, I_ROOT, n)
        }
        ip(i, I_DEPTH, d + 1)
    }
    let d = ig(i, I_DEPTH)
    if d == 0 {
        if ig(i, I_ROOT) != 0 {
            return ig(i, I_ROOT)
        }
        let pa = data_frame(i, pg)
        ip(i, I_ROOT, pa)
        return pa
    }
    if ig(i, I_ROOT) == 0 {
        let n = grab()
        if n == 0 {
            return 0
        }
        ip(i, I_ROOT, n)
    }
    var tbl = ig(i, I_ROOT)
    var idx = pg
    if d == 2 {
        let at = tbl + hh() + (pg / PTRS) * 8
        let m = rd(at)
        if m == 0 {
            let n = grab()
            if n == 0 {
                return 0
            }
            wr(at, n)
            tbl = n
        } else {
            tbl = m
        }
        idx = pg % PTRS
    }
    let cur = rd(tbl + hh() + idx * 8)
    if cur != 0 {
        return cur
    }
    let pa = data_frame(i, pg)
    if pa != 0 {
        wr(tbl + hh() + idx * 8, pa)
    }
    pa
}

/// Give back the data frames a leaf table at `tbl` points to from slot
/// `lo` on.
fn free_leaves(i: u64, tbl: u64, lo: u64) {
    var k = lo
    while k < PTRS {
        let at = tbl + hh() + k * 8
        let pa = rd(at)
        if pa != 0 {
            give(pa)
            wr(at, 0)
            ip(i, I_BLOCKS, ig(i, I_BLOCKS) - 1)
        }
        k += 1
    }
}

/// Inode `i` keeps only its first `size` bytes: every frame past them
/// goes back (an index frame with its last pointer), the page that
/// stays is zeroed past them, and the archive is read no further.
fn cut(i: u64, size: u64) {
    let keep = (size + PAGE - 1) / PAGE
    let d = ig(i, I_DEPTH)
    let root = ig(i, I_ROOT)
    if root != 0 {
        if d == 0 {
            if keep == 0 {
                give(root)
                ip(i, I_BLOCKS, ig(i, I_BLOCKS) - 1)
                ip(i, I_ROOT, 0)
            }
        } else if d == 1 {
            if keep < PTRS {
                free_leaves(i, root, keep)
            }
            if keep == 0 {
                give(root)
                ip(i, I_ROOT, 0)
            }
        } else {
            var m = keep / PTRS
            while m < PTRS {
                let at = root + hh() + m * 8
                let mid = rd(at)
                if mid != 0 {
                    let lo = if m == keep / PTRS { keep % PTRS } else { 0 }
                    free_leaves(i, mid, lo)
                    if lo == 0 {
                        give(mid)
                        wr(at, 0)
                    }
                }
                m += 1
            }
            if keep == 0 {
                give(root)
                ip(i, I_ROOT, 0)
            }
        }
    }
    if keep == 0 {
        ip(i, I_DEPTH, 0)
    }
    if size % PAGE != 0 {
        let pa = frame_of(i, size / PAGE)
        if pa != 0 {
            zero(pa + hh() + size % PAGE, PAGE - size % PAGE)
        }
    }
    if ig(i, I_BACKLEN) > size {
        ip(i, I_BACKLEN, size)
    }
}

/// Where up to `want` bytes of file `i` at offset `off` are, in kernel
/// memory: (the address, how many): a frame's, the archive's, or the
/// page of zeros for a hole. Never past a page; the caller keeps
/// `off + want` within the file's size.
pub fn span(i: u64, off: u64, want: u64) -> (u64, u64) {
    let po = off % PAGE
    var n = PAGE - po
    if want < n {
        n = want
    }
    let pa = frame_of(i, off / PAGE)
    if pa != 0 {
        return (pa + hh() + po, n)
    }
    if on_volume(i) {
        return ext2.rspan(vol(i), vino(i), off, n) // px63: (0, 0) on an I/O error
    }
    let bl = ig(i, I_BACKLEN)
    if off < bl {
        if bl - off < n {
            n = bl - off
        }
        return (ig(i, I_BACK) + off, n)
    }
    (st(S_ZERO) + hh() + po, n)
}

/// A file's size in bytes (a directory's record bytes).
pub fn bytes(i: u64) -> u64 {
    if on_volume(i) {
        return ext2.size(vol(i), vino(i))
    }
    ig(i, I_SIZE)
}

/// px62: the frame holding page `pg` of file `i` (a mapping's fault,
/// kernel/vm: the tree's own frames are the page cache, the only copy
/// of the file's bytes), made when there is none: the archive's bytes
/// copied into it, as a first write copies them, or zeros for a hole.
/// 0 at the cap, or past the largest file.
pub fn page(i: u64, pg: u64) -> u64 {
    if pg >= PTRS * PTRS {
        return 0
    }
    frame_for(i, pg)
}

/// px62: page `pg` of file `i`, all 4096 bytes, copied to the kernel
/// address `dst` (a frame through the HHDM): a frame's whole page, the
/// archive's bytes with zeros after them, or zeros (a hole, or past the
/// end). The copy a private mapping's page becomes when it is written,
/// or when the tree has no frame to share.
pub fn read_page(i: u64, pg: u64, dst: u64) {
    let pa = frame_of(i, pg)
    if pa != 0 {
        bcopy(dst, pa + hh(), PAGE)
        return
    }
    zero(dst, PAGE)
    if on_volume(i) {
        vfill(i, pg, dst)
        return
    }
    let bl = ig(i, I_BACKLEN)
    if pg * PAGE < bl {
        let n = if bl - pg * PAGE < PAGE { bl - pg * PAGE } else { PAGE }
        bcopy(dst, ig(i, I_BACK) + pg * PAGE, n)
    }
}

/// Copy `n` kernel bytes at `src` into the user range at `dst`, which
/// the caller has checked writable in `pml4`.
fn to_user(pml4: u64, dst: u64, src: u64, n: u64) {
    var k: u64 = 0
    while k < n {
        let room = PAGE - (dst + k) % PAGE
        let c = if n - k < room { n - k } else { room }
        let pa = paging.translate(pml4, dst + k) else 0
        bcopy(pa + hh(), src + k, c)
        k += c
    }
}

/// Copy `n` user bytes at `src` (checked readable) to kernel `dst`.
fn from_user(pml4: u64, dst: u64, src: u64, n: u64) {
    var k: u64 = 0
    while k < n {
        let room = PAGE - (src + k) % PAGE
        let c = if n - k < room { n - k } else { room }
        let pa = paging.translate(pml4, src + k) else 0
        bcopy(dst + k, pa + hh(), c)
        k += c
    }
}

/// Read up to `n` bytes of file `i` from `off` into the user buffer
/// `buf`, which the caller has checked writable for the bytes there
/// are: the count (0 at or past the end).
pub fn read(pml4: u64, i: u64, off: u64, buf: u64, n: u64) -> u64 {
    let size = bytes(i)
    if off >= size || n == 0 {
        return 0
    }
    let k = if n < size - off { n } else { size - off }
    var done: u64 = 0
    while done < k {
        let (src, c) = span(i, off + done, k - done)
        if c == 0 {
            break // px63: a volume's I/O error
        }
        to_user(pml4, buf + done, src, c)
        done += c
    }
    if done == 0 {
        return neg(EIO)
    }
    touch_read(i)
    done
}

/// Write `n` bytes into file `i` at `off`, from the user buffer `buf`
/// (checked readable by the caller) when `pml4` is not 0, else from
/// kernel memory at `buf`: the count written, which is less than `n`
/// when the tree's frames ran out part-way (`write(2)`); -ENOSPC when
/// none could be written; -EFBIG at the largest file.
pub fn write(pml4: u64, i: u64, off: u64, buf: u64, n: u64) -> u64 {
    if n == 0 {
        return 0
    }
    if on_volume(i) {
        return vwrite(pml4, i, off, buf, n)
    }
    if off >= MAX_SIZE {
        return neg(EFBIG)
    }
    let k = if n < MAX_SIZE - off { n } else { MAX_SIZE - off }
    var done: u64 = 0
    while done < k {
        let po = (off + done) % PAGE
        let c = if k - done < PAGE - po { k - done } else { PAGE - po }
        let pa = frame_for(i, (off + done) / PAGE)
        if pa == 0 {
            break
        }
        if pml4 != 0 {
            from_user(pml4, pa + hh() + po, buf + done, c)
        } else {
            bcopy(pa + hh() + po, buf + done, c)
        }
        done += c
    }
    if done == 0 {
        return neg(ENOSPC)
    }
    if off + done > ig(i, I_SIZE) {
        ip(i, I_SIZE, off + done)
    }
    touch_change(i)
    done
}

/// `ftruncate`: file `i` is `size` bytes long: cut (its frames past
/// that given back), or longer by a hole. -EFBIG past the largest file.
pub fn truncate(i: u64, size: u64) -> u64 {
    if on_volume(i) {
        return vtruncate(i, size)
    }
    if size > MAX_SIZE {
        return neg(EFBIG)
    }
    let old = ig(i, I_SIZE)
    if size < old {
        cut(i, size)
    }
    ip(i, I_SIZE, size)
    touch_change(i)
    0
}

/// px49 (pax#63): `fallocate`'s FALLOC_FL_PUNCH_HOLE with
/// FALLOC_FL_KEEP_SIZE: the bytes of file `i` in [off, off + len) that
/// lie inside its size read as zero afterwards; the size is kept. A
/// page with no frame is a hole already; the frames under the range are
/// kept, zeroed (named: tmpfs gives a whole page back, so `st_blocks`
/// is not Linux's after a punch).
pub fn punch(i: u64, off: u64, len: u64) {
    let size = bytes(i)
    if on_volume(i) && off < size {
        let end = if len < size - off { off + len } else { size }
        ext2.zero_range(vol(i), vino(i), off, end - off) // px63: the blocks kept, zeroed
    }
    if off >= size {
        touch_change(i)
        return
    }
    let end = if len < size - off { off + len } else { size }
    var p = off
    while p < end {
        let po = p % PAGE
        let c = if end - p < PAGE - po { end - p } else { PAGE - po }
        let pa = frame_of(i, p / PAGE)
        if pa != 0 {
            zero(pa + hh() + po, c)
        }
        p += c
    }
    touch_change(i)
}

// --- directories -----------------------------------------------------------------

fn need(len: u64) -> u64 {
    (8 + len + 7) & !7
}

fn same(a: u64, b: u64, n: u64) -> bool {
    var k: u64 = 0
    while k < n {
        if rd8(a + k) != rd8(b + k) {
            return false
        }
        k += 1
    }
    true
}

/// The record of the name [name, name + len) in directory `d`: its
/// kernel address, or 0.
fn find(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64) -> u64 {
    let size = ig(d, I_SIZE)
    var pg: u64 = 0
    while pg * PAGE < size {
        let pa = frame_of(d, pg)
        if pa != 0 {
            let b = pa + hh()
            var o: u64 = 0
            while o < PAGE {
                let rl = rd16(b + o + 4)
                if rl == 0 {
                    break
                }
                if rd32(b + o) != 0 && rd16(b + o + 6) == len && same(b + o + 8, name, len) {
                    return b + o
                }
                o += rl
            }
        }
        pg += 1
    }
    0
}

/// The inode the name [name, name + len) leads to in directory `d`, or
/// NONE (also in a directory that has been removed).
pub fn lookup(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64) -> u64 {
    var i = NONE
    if on_volume(d) {
        let n = ext2.lookup(vol(d), vino(d), name, len)
        if n == 0 {
            return NONE
        }
        i = vrec(vol(d), n, d)
    } else {
        let r = find(d, name, len)
        if r == 0 {
            return NONE
        }
        i = rd32(r) - 1
    }
    if i != NONE && is_point(i) {
        return mw(point_mount(i), M_ROOT) // px63: a mount point leads to the volume's root
    }
    i
}

/// Fill the free record at `r` (of `rl` bytes) with the name and inode,
/// leaving what it does not need free.
fn fill(r: u64, rl: u64, name: u64, len: u64, ino: u64) {
    let nd = need(len)
    if rl - nd >= 16 {
        wr32(r + nd, 0)
        wr16(r + nd + 4, rl - nd)
        wr16(r + nd + 6, 0)
        wr16(r + 4, nd)
    }
    wr16(r + 6, len)
    bcopy(r + 8, name, len)
    wr32(r, ino + 1)
}

/// A record for the name in directory `d`, leading to `ino`: false
/// when a new page was needed and the tree is at its cap.
fn insert(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64, ino: u64) -> bool {
    let nd = need(len)
    let size = ig(d, I_SIZE)
    var pg: u64 = 0
    while pg * PAGE < size {
        let pa = frame_of(d, pg)
        if pa != 0 {
            let b = pa + hh()
            var o: u64 = 0
            while o < PAGE {
                let rl = rd16(b + o + 4)
                if rl == 0 {
                    break
                }
                if rd32(b + o) == 0 && rl >= nd {
                    fill(b + o, rl, name, len, ino)
                    return true
                }
                o += rl
            }
        }
        pg += 1
    }
    let pa = frame_for(d, size / PAGE)
    if pa == 0 {
        return false
    }
    let b = pa + hh()
    wr32(b, 0)
    wr16(b + 4, PAGE)
    wr16(b + 6, 0)
    fill(b, PAGE, name, len, ino)
    ip(d, I_SIZE, size + PAGE)
    true
}

/// The record at `r` is free again, and joins the free records after
/// it on its page; a directory left with no entry gives its pages back.
fn remove(d: u64, r: u64) {
    wr32(r, 0)
    let b = r & !(PAGE - 1)
    var o: u64 = 0
    while o < PAGE {
        var rl = rd16(b + o + 4)
        if rl == 0 {
            break
        }
        if rd32(b + o) == 0 {
            while o + rl < PAGE && rd32(b + o + rl) == 0 && rd16(b + o + rl + 4) != 0 {
                rl += rd16(b + o + rl + 4)
                wr16(b + o + 4, rl)
            }
        }
        o += rl
    }
    ip(d, I_ENTRIES, ig(d, I_ENTRIES) - 1)
    if ig(d, I_ENTRIES) == 0 {
        cut(d, 0)
        ip(d, I_SIZE, 0)
    }
}

/// The first entry of directory `d` at or after position `pos` (a
/// record's offset, found from its page's start, so a position stays
/// good while the directory changes): (the inode or NONE at the end,
/// the name's kernel address, its length, the position after it).
pub fn entry_at(d: u64, pos: u64) -> (u64, u64, u64, u64) {
    let size = ig(d, I_SIZE)
    var pg = pos / PAGE
    var want = pos % PAGE
    while pg * PAGE < size {
        let pa = frame_of(d, pg)
        if pa != 0 {
            let b = pa + hh()
            var o: u64 = 0
            while o < PAGE {
                let rl = rd16(b + o + 4)
                if rl == 0 {
                    break
                }
                if o >= want && rd32(b + o) != 0 {
                    return (rd32(b + o) - 1, b + o + 8, rd16(b + o + 6), pg * PAGE + o + rl)
                }
                o += rl
            }
        }
        pg += 1
        want = 0
    }
    (NONE, 0, 0, size)
}

/// The name directory `d` gives its child `c`: (its kernel address,
/// its length), or (0, 0) when `c` has no name there (a removed
/// directory).
pub fn name_of(d: u64, c: u64) -> (u64, u64) {
    let m = root_of(c)
    if m != MOUNTS {
        return name_of(d, mw(m, M_POINT) - 1) // px63: a mount's root: the covered directory's name
    }
    if on_volume(d) {
        if !on_volume(c) || vol(c) != vol(d) {
            return (0, 0)
        }
        return ext2.name_of(vol(d), vino(d), vino(c))
    }
    var pos: u64 = 0
    var ra: u64 = 0
    var rl: u64 = 0
    var more = true
    while more {
        let (i, a, l, next) = entry_at(d, pos)
        if i == NONE {
            more = false
        } else if i == c {
            ra = a
            rl = l
            more = false
        } else {
            pos = next
        }
    }
    (ra, rl)
}

/// A new file named [name, name + len) in directory `d`, with the
/// permission bits `perm`, owned `uid`:`gid` (px42): its inode, or
/// -ENOENT (the directory has been removed), -ENOSPC.
pub fn create(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64, perm: u64, uid: u64, gid: u64) -> u64 {
    make(d, name, len, S_IFREG | (perm & 0xfff), uid, gid)
}

/// px63: `create`'s, for a mode of any type (a regular file, a socket's
/// name, a FIFO): on a volume the type is the inode's and the entry's
/// from the start.
fn make(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64, m: u64, uid: u64, gid: u64) -> u64 {
    if on_volume(d) {
        return vmake(d, name, len, m, uid, gid)
    }
    if ig(d, I_NLINK) == 0 {
        return neg(ENOENT)
    }
    let i = inode_new(m, uid, gid)
    if i == NONE {
        return neg(ENOSPC)
    }
    if !insert(d, name, len, i) {
        ip(i, I_NLINK, 0)
        inode_free(i)
        return neg(ENOSPC)
    }
    ip(i, I_NLINK, 1)
    ip(d, I_ENTRIES, ig(d, I_ENTRIES) + 1)
    touch_change(d)
    i
}

/// px34: a socket's name [name, name + len) in directory `d` (`bind` on
/// an AF_UNIX path socket), mode S_IFSOCK with the permission bits
/// `perm`, size 0, one link, owned `uid`:`gid` (px42), naming socket
/// record `sock` (kernel/unix): its inode, or -ENOENT (the directory
/// has been removed), -ENOSPC.
pub fn mksock(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64, perm: u64, sock: u64, uid: u64, gid: u64) -> u64 {
    let i = make(d, name, len, S_IFSOCK | (perm & 0xfff), uid, gid)
    if failed(i) {
        return i
    }
    ip(i, I_PARENT, sock + 1)
    i
}

/// px62: a FIFO's name [name, name + len) in directory `d` (`mknod(2)`
/// and `mkfifo(3)`, fifo(7)): mode S_IFIFO with the permission bits
/// `perm`, size 0, one link, owned `uid`:`gid`; its inode, or -ENOENT
/// (the directory has been removed), -ENOSPC. It holds no bytes: what
/// is written to it goes through the pipe buffer its open ends share
/// (kernel/files'), whose record + 1 is in the word a socket's name
/// keeps its record in (`fifo_pipe`), and how many times each end has
/// been opened is in the word a directory counts its entries in
/// (`fifo_opens`).
pub fn mkfifo(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64, perm: u64, uid: u64, gid: u64) -> u64 {
    make(d, name, len, S_IFIFO | (perm & 0xfff), uid, gid)
}

/// px62: whether inode `i` is a FIFO.
pub fn is_fifo(i: u64) -> bool {
    ig(i, I_MODE) & S_IFMT == S_IFIFO
}

/// px62: the pipe buffer FIFO `i`'s open ends share (kernel/files'
/// record + 1), 0 while no end is open.
pub fn fifo_pipe(i: u64) -> u64 {
    if !is_fifo(i) {
        return 0
    }
    ig(i, I_PARENT)
}

pub fn set_fifo_pipe(i: u64, p: u64) {
    if is_fifo(i) {
        ip(i, I_PARENT, p)
    }
}

/// px62: how many times FIFO `i` has been opened for reading (`which`
/// 0) or for writing (1) since it was made, 32 bits each: a waiting
/// open of one end goes on once the other end's count has moved
/// (fifo(7): it waits for the other end to be opened, not to stay
/// open).
pub fn fifo_opens(i: u64, which: int) -> u64 {
    let w = ig(i, I_ENTRIES)
    if which == 0 { w & 0xffffffff } else { w >> 32 }
}

pub fn fifo_opened(i: u64, which: int) {
    let w = ig(i, I_ENTRIES)
    let lo = w & 0xffffffff
    let hi = w >> 32
    if which == 0 {
        ip(i, I_ENTRIES, ((lo + 1) & 0xffffffff) | (hi << 32))
    } else {
        ip(i, I_ENTRIES, lo | (((hi + 1) & 0xffffffff) << 32))
    }
}

/// px62: an inode with no name for shared memory that is no file's
/// (`mmap(2)`'s MAP_SHARED|MAP_ANONYMOUS, and MAP_SHARED of /dev/zero):
/// a regular file of `size` bytes, mode 0600, owned `uid`:`gid`, no
/// link: kernel/vm's mapping holds it (`hold`), and its frames go back
/// with the last mapping (`release`). Its index, or NONE.
pub fn anon(size: u64, uid: u64, gid: u64) -> u64 {
    let i = inode_new(S_IFREG | 0x180, uid, gid)
    if i == NONE {
        return NONE
    }
    ip(i, I_SIZE, size)
    i
}

/// px36: whether inode `i` is a symbolic link.
pub fn is_link(i: u64) -> bool {
    ig(i, I_MODE) & S_IFMT == S_IFLNK
}

/// px36: a new symbolic link named [name, name + len) in directory `d`
/// whose target is the `tlen` kernel bytes at `target` (1 to 4095:
/// the caller has refused the rest): mode S_IFLNK|0777 (`symlink(7)`:
/// a link's permission bits are not used), one link, its bytes the
/// target's, held as a file's are, owned `uid`:`gid` (px42); its inode,
/// or -ENOENT (the directory has been removed), -ENOSPC.
pub fn symlink(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64, target: u64, tlen: u64, uid: u64, gid: u64) -> u64 {
    if on_volume(d) {
        return vsymlink(d, name, len, target, tlen, uid, gid)
    }
    if ig(d, I_NLINK) == 0 {
        return neg(ENOENT)
    }
    let i = inode_new(S_IFLNK | 0x1ff, uid, gid)
    if i == NONE {
        return neg(ENOSPC)
    }
    let w = write(0, i, 0, target, tlen)
    if w != tlen || !insert(d, name, len, i) {
        inode_free(i)
        return neg(ENOSPC)
    }
    let t = ig(i, I_BTIME)
    ip(i, I_MTIME, t) // `write` stamped them again; one time, as made
    ip(i, I_CTIME, t)
    ip(i, I_NLINK, 1)
    ip(d, I_ENTRIES, ig(d, I_ENTRIES) + 1)
    touch_change(d)
    i
}

/// px36: copy at most `n` bytes of link `i`'s target to kernel `dst`:
/// how many.
pub fn target(i: u64, dst: u64, n: u64) -> u64 {
    if on_volume(i) {
        return ext2.target(vol(i), vino(i), dst, n)
    }
    let k = if n < ig(i, I_SIZE) { n } else { ig(i, I_SIZE) }
    var done: u64 = 0
    while done < k {
        let (src, c) = span(i, done, k - done)
        bcopy(dst + done, src, c)
        done += c
    }
    k
}

/// px36: `link`: inode `i` (a file or a link, never a directory) gains
/// the name [name, name + len) in directory `d`: its count up, its
/// ctime and the directory's times moved. 0, or -ENOENT (the directory
/// has been removed, or the file has no name left), -ENOSPC.
pub fn link(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64, i: u64) -> u64 {
    if store(d) != store(i) {
        return neg(EXDEV) // px63: a name on another store
    }
    if on_volume(d) {
        return vlink(d, name, len, i)
    }
    if ig(d, I_NLINK) == 0 || ig(i, I_NLINK) == 0 {
        return neg(ENOENT)
    }
    if !insert(d, name, len, i) {
        return neg(ENOSPC)
    }
    ip(i, I_NLINK, ig(i, I_NLINK) + 1)
    ip(i, I_CTIME, now())
    ip(d, I_ENTRIES, ig(d, I_ENTRIES) + 1)
    touch_change(d)
    0
}

/// px36: `chmod`: inode `i`'s twelve permission bits become `perm`'s,
/// its type kept; ctime moves.
pub fn set_mode(i: u64, perm: u64) {
    ip(i, I_MODE, (ig(i, I_MODE) & S_IFMT) | (perm & 0xfff))
    if on_volume(i) {
        vmode(i)
        return
    }
    ip(i, I_CTIME, now())
}

/// `chown` (px36's `owned`; px42: any id): inode `i`'s owner becomes
/// `uid` and its group `gid`, each left as it is when KEEP (-1); ctime
/// moves, and a regular file loses its set-user-ID bit and, when it is
/// group-executable, its set-group-ID bit (measured on tmpfs for root
/// and for an owner alike, px38's `perm` section E), whichever ids
/// were asked for, -1 and -1 included. A directory's bits and the
/// sticky bit stay. `outside`: the caller is neither privileged nor in
/// the group the file has, and the set-group-ID bit then goes whether
/// or not the file is group-executable (measured: an owner outside the
/// group turns 2644 into 0644 with `chown(-1, -1)`; one inside it, and
/// root, leave it). Who may ask is the caller's to decide.
pub fn chown(i: u64, uid: u64, gid: u64, outside: bool) {
    let (ou, og) = owner_of(i)
    let u = if uid & 0xffffffff == KEEP { ou } else { uid }
    let g = if gid & 0xffffffff == KEEP { og } else { gid }
    if on_volume(i) {
        ext2.set_owner(vol(i), vino(i), u, g)
    }
    ip(i, I_OWNER, pack(u, g))
    let m = ig(i, I_MODE)
    if m & S_IFMT == S_IFREG {
        var keep = m & !S_ISUID
        if m & S_IXGRP != 0 || outside {
            keep = keep & !S_ISGID
        }
        ip(i, I_MODE, keep)
    }
    if on_volume(i) {
        vmode(i)
        return
    }
    ip(i, I_CTIME, now())
}

/// px36: `utimensat`: inode `i`'s access time becomes `at` when `which`
/// has bit 0, its modification time `mt` when it has bit 1 (signed
/// nanoseconds since the epoch, to the nanosecond); ctime moves to now
/// when either does.
pub fn set_times(i: u64, at: u64, mt: u64, which: u64) {
    if on_volume(i) {
        if ext2.read_only(vol(i)) == 0 {
            ext2.set_times(vol(i), vino(i), at, mt, now(), which)
        }
        return
    }
    if which & 1 != 0 {
        ip(i, I_ATIME, at)
    }
    if which & 2 != 0 {
        ip(i, I_MTIME, mt)
    }
    if which != 0 {
        ip(i, I_CTIME, now())
    }
}

/// px36: the wall clock as the tree stamps a change (`UTIME_NOW`).
pub fn clock() -> u64 {
    now()
}

/// px34: whether inode `i` is a socket's name.
pub fn is_sock(i: u64) -> bool {
    ig(i, I_MODE) & S_IFMT == S_IFSOCK
}

/// px34: the socket record a socket's name leads to, + 1; 0 when the
/// socket it named has closed (connect is then refused, unix(7)).
pub fn sock_of(i: u64) -> u64 {
    if !is_sock(i) {
        return 0
    }
    ig(i, I_PARENT)
}

/// px34: the socket the name led to has closed: the name stays, leading
/// nowhere, until it is unlinked.
pub fn sock_gone(i: u64) {
    if is_sock(i) {
        ip(i, I_PARENT, 0)
    }
}

/// A new directory named [name, name + len) in directory `d`, owned
/// `uid`:`gid` (px42): its inode, or -ENOENT, -ENOSPC.
pub fn mkdir(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64, perm: u64, uid: u64, gid: u64) -> u64 {
    if on_volume(d) {
        return vmkdir(d, name, len, perm, uid, gid)
    }
    if ig(d, I_NLINK) == 0 {
        return neg(ENOENT)
    }
    let i = inode_new(S_IFDIR | (perm & 0xfff), uid, gid)
    if i == NONE {
        return neg(ENOSPC)
    }
    ip(i, I_PARENT, i) // until it has one: inode_free releases no parent
    if !insert(d, name, len, i) {
        inode_free(i)
        return neg(ENOSPC)
    }
    ip(i, I_PARENT, d)
    ip(i, I_NLINK, 2)
    ip(d, I_NLINK, ig(d, I_NLINK) + 1)
    ip(d, I_ENTRIES, ig(d, I_ENTRIES) + 1)
    touch_change(d)
    i
}

/// File inode `i` loses a name: its count drops, and with no name and
/// no holder left it is freed.
fn drop_file(i: u64) {
    ip(i, I_NLINK, ig(i, I_NLINK) - 1)
    ip(i, I_CTIME, now())
    if ig(i, I_NLINK) == 0 && ig(i, I_REFS) == 0 {
        inode_free(i)
    }
}

/// Directory inode `i` (empty) loses its name in `d`: no link left; it
/// lives on, empty, while a process works in it or has it open, holding
/// its parent so `..` still leads there.
fn drop_dir(d: u64, i: u64) {
    ip(d, I_NLINK, ig(d, I_NLINK) - 1)
    ip(i, I_NLINK, 0)
    ip(i, I_CTIME, now())
    if ig(i, I_REFS) == 0 {
        ip(i, I_PARENT, i)
        inode_free(i)
    } else {
        hold(d)
    }
}

/// `unlink`: the name in directory `d` is removed: 0, -ENOENT, -EISDIR.
pub fn unlink(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64) -> u64 {
    if on_volume(d) {
        return vunlink(d, name, len)
    }
    let r = find(d, name, len)
    if r == 0 {
        return neg(ENOENT)
    }
    let i = rd32(r) - 1
    if is_dir(i) {
        return neg(EISDIR)
    }
    remove(d, r)
    touch_change(d)
    drop_file(i)
    put_st(S_UNLINKS, st(S_UNLINKS) + 1)
    0
}

/// `rmdir`: the empty directory named in `d` is removed: 0, -ENOENT,
/// -ENOTDIR, -ENOTEMPTY.
pub fn rmdir(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64) -> u64 {
    if on_volume(d) {
        return vrmdir(d, name, len)
    }
    let r = find(d, name, len)
    if r == 0 {
        return neg(ENOENT)
    }
    let i = rd32(r) - 1
    if !is_dir(i) {
        return neg(ENOTDIR)
    }
    if is_point(i) {
        return neg(EBUSY) // px63: a volume is mounted on it
    }
    if ig(i, I_ENTRIES) != 0 {
        return neg(ENOTEMPTY)
    }
    remove(d, r)
    touch_change(d)
    drop_dir(d, i)
    0
}

/// Whether directory `d` is `a` or lies below it.
fn below(d: u64, a: u64) -> bool {
    var c = d
    var found = c == a
    while !found && parent(c) != c {
        c = parent(c)
        found = c == a
    }
    found
}

/// `rename`: the name [on, on + ol) in directory `od` becomes [nn, nn +
/// nl) in directory `nd`, replacing what is there. Every refusal is
/// decided and the room for the new name found before anything
/// changes: 0, -ENOENT, -EINVAL (a directory into itself or below
/// itself), -EISDIR, -ENOTDIR, -ENOTEMPTY, -ENOSPC.
pub fn rename(od: u64, on: u64, ol: u64, nd: u64, nn: u64, nl: u64) -> u64 {
    if store(od) != store(nd) {
        return neg(EXDEV) // px63
    }
    if on_volume(od) {
        return vrename(od, on, ol, nd, nn, nl)
    }
    let r = find(od, on, ol)
    if r == 0 || ig(nd, I_NLINK) == 0 {
        return neg(ENOENT)
    }
    let i = rd32(r) - 1
    if is_point(i) {
        return neg(EBUSY) // px63: a volume is mounted on it
    }
    let dir = is_dir(i)
    if dir && below(nd, i) {
        return neg(EINVAL)
    }
    let t = find(nd, nn, nl)
    if t != 0 {
        let j = rd32(t) - 1
        if j == i {
            return 0
        }
        if is_point(j) {
            return neg(EBUSY) // px63
        }
        if dir && !is_dir(j) {
            return neg(ENOTDIR)
        }
        if !dir && is_dir(j) {
            return neg(EISDIR)
        }
        if dir && ig(j, I_ENTRIES) != 0 {
            return neg(ENOTEMPTY)
        }
        // The change: the new name leads to the moved inode, the old
        // name goes, what was there loses its name.
        // (`remove` counts the old directory's entries one down; the
        // new one's are as many as before.)
        wr32(t, i + 1)
        remove(od, r)
        if dir {
            drop_dir(nd, j)
        } else {
            drop_file(j)
        }
    } else {
        if !insert(nd, nn, nl, i) {
            return neg(ENOSPC)
        }
        ip(nd, I_ENTRIES, ig(nd, I_ENTRIES) + 1)
        // `insert` may have filled a record on the old name's page, never
        // the old record itself (it was not free).
        remove(od, find(od, on, ol))
    }
    if dir && od != nd {
        ip(od, I_NLINK, ig(od, I_NLINK) - 1)
        ip(nd, I_NLINK, ig(nd, I_NLINK) + 1)
        ip(i, I_PARENT, nd)
    }
    touch_change(od)
    touch_change(nd)
    ip(i, I_CTIME, now())
    0
}

// --- px63: the second store, ext2 volumes ------------------------------------------

// The volumes' frame (S_VOLF), words: the mount table, the side
// table's frames, the hash's frames, the eviction cursor.
const VF_MOUNT: u64 = 0 // MOUNTS records of MW words
/// The most mounts at once (px67: 8; px63's 4): a volume's, or (px67)
/// a directory of the memory's mounted over a volume's (`/tmp`).
pub const MOUNTS: u64 = 8
const MW: u64 = 8
const M_POINT: u64 = 0 // the covered directory + 1; 0 a free record
const M_ROOT: u64 = 1 // the mount's root's record: the volume's root, or the memory's directory
const M_VOL: u64 = 2 // kernel/ext2's volume; px67: NONE, the memory's
const M_DEV: u64 = 3 // kernel/block's disk (a volume's)
const M_SEQ: u64 = 4 // px67: the order it was mounted in (1, 2, …): the halt's reverse order, /proc/self/mounts' order
const M_HOW: u64 = 5 // px67: what kernel/fstab or mount(2) asked (MH_*), for /proc/self/mounts
const VF_SIDE: u64 = 64 // the side table's frames, SIDE_FRAMES of them
const SIDE_FRAMES: u64 = 32 // MAX_INODES / 512
const SIDE_PER: u64 = 512
const VF_HASH: u64 = 96 // the hash's two frames: BUCKETS chain heads (a record + 1)
const BUCKETS: u64 = 1024
const VF_CURSOR: u64 = 98
const VF_SEQ: u64 = 99 // px67: the last mount's M_SEQ
/// px67: M_HOW's bits: the volume is written through (`sync`); it was
/// mounted by `root=` (its source reads `/dev/root`, as Linux names it).
pub const MH_SYNC: u64 = 1
pub const MH_ROOT: u64 = 2
pub const MH_NOSUID: u64 = 4
pub const MH_NODEV: u64 = 8
pub const MH_NOEXEC: u64 = 16
const M_MODE: u64 = 6 // px67: a memory mount's directory's mode as asked (`mode=`), for /proc/self/mounts
/// Records of a volume's inodes kept while nobody holds them before the
/// oldest are given back.
pub const VOL_KEEP: u64 = 2048

// A side word: the ext2 inode number (bits 0-31), the volume + 1 (bits
// 32-35; 0: a record of the memory), a shared writable mapping has had
// its pages (bit 36), the record is a mount point (bit 37) and which
// (bits 38-39), the system call it was last looked up in modulo 128
// (bits 41-47), the hash chain's next record + 1 (bits 48-63). px67:
// which mount, bits 38-40 (MOUNTS is 8).
const SD_VOL_SHIFT: u64 = 32
const SD_SHARED: u64 = 0x1000000000
const SD_POINT: u64 = 0x2000000000
const SD_MOUNT_SHIFT: u64 = 38
const SD_GEN_SHIFT: u64 = 41
const SD_NEXT_SHIFT: u64 = 48

fn vf(w: u64) -> u64 {
    let f = st(S_VOLF)
    if f == 0 { 0 } else { rd(f + hh() + w * 8) }
}

fn put_vf(w: u64, v: u64) {
    wr(st(S_VOLF) + hh() + w * 8, v)
}

fn mw(m: u64, w: u64) -> u64 {
    vf(VF_MOUNT + m * MW + w)
}

fn put_mw(m: u64, w: u64, v: u64) {
    put_vf(VF_MOUNT + m * MW + w, v)
}

fn side_addr(i: u64) -> u64 {
    let f = vf(VF_SIDE + i / SIDE_PER)
    if f == 0 { 0 } else { f + hh() + (i % SIDE_PER) * 8 }
}

fn side(i: u64) -> u64 {
    let a = side_addr(i)
    if a == 0 { 0 } else { rd(a) }
}

fn put_side(i: u64, v: u64) {
    let a = side_addr(i)
    if a != 0 {
        wr(a, v)
    }
}

/// px63: whether inode `i` is a volume's (kernel/ext2's), not the memory's.
pub fn on_volume(i: u64) -> bool {
    (side(i) >> SD_VOL_SHIFT) & 0xf != 0
}

fn vol(i: u64) -> u64 {
    ((side(i) >> SD_VOL_SHIFT) & 0xf) - 1
}

fn vino(i: u64) -> u64 {
    side(i) & 0xffffffff
}

fn is_point(i: u64) -> bool {
    side(i) & SD_POINT != 0
}

fn point_mount(i: u64) -> u64 {
    (side(i) >> SD_MOUNT_SHIFT) & 7
}

fn is_vroot(i: u64) -> bool {
    on_volume(i) && vino(i) == ext2.ROOT_INO
}

/// px63: the number `stat` answers for inode `i`: a volume's own inode
/// number, or the memory's index + 2 (px27: the root is 2, never 0).
pub fn number(i: u64) -> u64 {
    if on_volume(i) { vino(i) } else { i + 2 }
}

/// px63: which store inode `i` is in: 0 the memory, a volume's number + 1.
pub fn store(i: u64) -> u64 {
    (side(i) >> SD_VOL_SHIFT) & 0xf
}

/// px63: the disk (kernel/block's) of inode `i`'s volume; NONE for the memory.
pub fn disk_of(i: u64) -> u64 {
    if on_volume(i) { ext2.dev_of(vol(i)) } else { NONE }
}

/// px63: whether inode `i` is on a volume mounted read-only (kernel/files
/// answers a change -EROFS).
pub fn read_only(i: u64) -> bool {
    on_volume(i) && ext2.read_only(vol(i)) != 0
}

/// px63: the block size `stat` gives inode `i` (st_blksize).
pub fn io_size(i: u64) -> u64 {
    if on_volume(i) { ext2.block_size(vol(i)) } else { PAGE }
}

/// px63: one more system call (kernel/user, at every entry): a volume's
/// record looked up in an earlier one may be given back.
pub fn tick() {
    put_st(S_GEN, st(S_GEN) + 1)
}

fn stamp(i: u64) {
    put_side(i, (side(i) & !(0x7f << SD_GEN_SHIFT)) | ((st(S_GEN) & 0x7f) << SD_GEN_SHIFT))
}

fn bucket(v: u64, ino: u64) -> u64 {
    let h = ((ino & 0xffffffff) * 0x9e3779b1 + v) >> 11
    vf(VF_HASH + (h % BUCKETS) / SIDE_PER) + hh() + (h % SIDE_PER) * 8
}

fn now_s() -> u64 {
    let t = now()
    if t >= 0x8000000000000000 { 0 } else { t / NS_PER_SEC }
}

fn vframe() -> u64 {
    let pa = frames.alloc() else 0
    if pa != 0 {
        zero(pa + hh(), PAGE)
        put_st(S_VSIDE, st(S_VSIDE) + 1)
    }
    pa
}

/// The volumes' frame, the side table and the hash, made at the first
/// mount (35 frames, never given back): whether they are there.
fn vol_ready() -> bool {
    if st(S_VOLF) != 0 {
        return true
    }
    let f = vframe()
    if f == 0 {
        return false
    }
    put_st(S_VOLF, f)
    var k: u64 = 0
    while k < SIDE_FRAMES + 2 {
        let s = vframe()
        if s == 0 {
            return false
        }
        if k < SIDE_FRAMES {
            put_vf(VF_SIDE + k, s)
        } else {
            put_vf(VF_HASH + k - SIDE_FRAMES, s)
        }
        k += 1
    }
    true
}

/// The record standing for inode `ino` of volume `v`, made when there is
/// none (a directory's holds `parent`, the directory it was found in, so
/// `..` leads back while it lives), stamped with this system call; NONE
/// when the inode cannot be read or the table is full.
fn vrec(v: u64, ino: u64, parent: u64) -> u64 {
    let b = bucket(v, ino)
    var r = rd(b)
    var guard: u64 = 0
    while r != 0 && guard <= MAX_INODES {
        let i = r - 1
        let s = side(i)
        if s & 0xffffffff == ino && (s >> SD_VOL_SHIFT) & 0xf == v + 1 {
            stamp(i)
            return i
        }
        r = s >> SD_NEXT_SHIFT
        guard += 1
    }
    if st(S_VLIVE) >= VOL_KEEP {
        evict(VOL_KEEP / 8)
    }
    let m = ext2.mode(v, ino)
    if m == 0 {
        return NONE
    }
    let (u, g) = ext2.owner(v, ino)
    var i = inode_new(m, u, g)
    if i == NONE {
        evict(VOL_KEEP)
        i = inode_new(m, u, g)
        if i == NONE {
            return NONE
        }
    }
    put_st(S_LIVE, st(S_LIVE) - 1)
    put_st(S_VLIVE, st(S_VLIVE) + 1)
    ip(i, I_NLINK, ext2.nlink(v, ino))
    put_side(i, ino | ((v + 1) << SD_VOL_SHIFT) | (rd(b) << SD_NEXT_SHIFT))
    wr(b, i + 1)
    stamp(i)
    if m & S_IFMT == S_IFDIR && ino != ext2.ROOT_INO {
        ip(i, I_PARENT, parent)
        hold(parent)
    }
    i
}

fn unhash(i: u64) {
    let b = bucket(vol(i), vino(i))
    var r = rd(b)
    if r == i + 1 {
        wr(b, side(i) >> SD_NEXT_SHIFT)
        return
    }
    var guard: u64 = 0
    while r != 0 && guard <= MAX_INODES {
        let nx = side(r - 1) >> SD_NEXT_SHIFT
        if nx == i + 1 {
            let keep = side(r - 1) & 0xffffffffffff
            put_side(r - 1, keep | ((side(i) >> SD_NEXT_SHIFT) << SD_NEXT_SHIFT))
            return
        }
        r = nx
        guard += 1
    }
}

/// Record `i` (a volume's) given back, its inode left on the disk: a
/// shared mapping's pages written first, its frames freed, a
/// directory's parent let go.
fn vdrop(i: u64) {
    writeback(i)
    cut(i, 0)
    unhash(i)
    let dir = ig(i, I_MODE) & S_IFMT == S_IFDIR && !is_vroot(i)
    let p = ig(i, I_PARENT)
    put_side(i, 0)
    ip(i, I_MODE, 0)
    ip(i, I_NEXT, st(S_FREE))
    put_st(S_FREE, i + 1)
    put_st(S_VLIVE, st(S_VLIVE) - 1)
    if dir {
        release(p)
    }
}

/// Record `i`'s inode has no name and no holder left: off the disk (its
/// blocks and its number given back), then the record.
fn vgone(i: u64) {
    let v = vol(i)
    if ext2.read_only(v) == 0 {
        ext2.ifree(v, vino(i), now_s())
    }
    vdrop(i)
}

/// Give back up to `want` records of volumes that nobody holds and no
/// earlier part of this system call looked up (the oldest first, by a
/// cursor that goes round the table).
fn evict(want: u64) {
    let top = st(S_NEXT)
    var c = vf(VF_CURSOR)
    var seen: u64 = 0
    var done: u64 = 0
    while seen < top && done < want {
        if c >= top {
            c = 0
        }
        let s = side(c)
        if (s >> SD_VOL_SHIFT) & 0xf != 0 && ig(c, I_MODE) != 0 && ig(c, I_REFS) == 0 && s & 0xffffffff != ext2.ROOT_INO && ((s >> SD_GEN_SHIFT) & 0x7f) != (st(S_GEN) & 0x7f) {
            vdrop(c)
            put_st(S_VEVICT, st(S_VEVICT) + 1)
            done += 1
        }
        c += 1
        seen += 1
    }
    put_vf(VF_CURSOR, c)
}

/// Page `pg` of volume file `i` read from the disk into the kernel page
/// at `dst` (zeros where the file has none).
fn vfill(i: u64, pg: u64, dst: u64) {
    let sz = bytes(i)
    var o: u64 = 0
    while o < PAGE && pg * PAGE + o < sz {
        let want = if sz - (pg * PAGE + o) < PAGE - o { sz - (pg * PAGE + o) } else { PAGE - o }
        let (src, c) = ext2.rspan(vol(i), vino(i), pg * PAGE + o, want)
        if c == 0 {
            return
        }
        bcopy(dst + o, src, c)
        o += c
    }
}

/// px63: a shared writable mapping has had volume file `i`'s pages
/// (kernel/vm's fault): they are written to the disk at `msync`,
/// `fsync`, `sync` and when the record goes.
pub fn shared_write(i: u64) {
    if on_volume(i) {
        put_side(i, side(i) | SD_SHARED)
    }
}

/// px63: write the frames of volume file `i` a shared writable mapping
/// may have changed to the disk (every frame it holds: the page table's
/// dirty bit is not read).
pub fn writeback(i: u64) {
    if side(i) & SD_SHARED == 0 || !on_volume(i) || ext2.read_only(vol(i)) != 0 {
        return
    }
    let sz = bytes(i)
    var pg: u64 = 0
    while pg * PAGE < sz && pg < PTRS * PTRS {
        let pa = frame_of(i, pg)
        if pa != 0 {
            let end = if sz - pg * PAGE < PAGE { sz - pg * PAGE } else { PAGE }
            var o: u64 = 0
            while o < end {
                let (dst, c, blk) = ext2.wspan(vol(i), vino(i), pg * PAGE + o, end - o)
                if c == 0 {
                    return
                }
                bcopy(dst, pa + hh() + o, c)
                ext2.wrote(vol(i), blk)
                o += c
            }
        }
        pg += 1
    }
}

/// `write` on a volume: block by block through kernel/ext2 (a block made
/// where there was none), a mapped page's frame kept in step; the size
/// and the times moved. The count, or -ENOSPC, -EIO, -EFBIG, -EROFS.
fn vwrite(pml4: u64, i: u64, off: u64, buf: u64, n: u64) -> u64 {
    let v = vol(i)
    let ino = vino(i)
    if ext2.read_only(v) != 0 {
        return neg(EROFS)
    }
    let max = ext2.max_size(v)
    if off >= max {
        return neg(EFBIG)
    }
    let k = if n < max - off { n } else { max - off }
    var done: u64 = 0
    while done < k {
        let (dst, c, blk) = ext2.wspan(v, ino, off + done, k - done)
        if c == 0 {
            break
        }
        if pml4 != 0 {
            from_user(pml4, dst, buf + done, c)
        } else {
            bcopy(dst, buf + done, c)
        }
        let pa = frame_of(i, (off + done) / PAGE)
        if pa != 0 {
            bcopy(pa + hh() + (off + done) % PAGE, dst, c)
        }
        ext2.wrote(v, blk)
        done += c
    }
    if done == 0 {
        return if ext2.full(v) { neg(ENOSPC) } else { neg(EIO) }
    }
    if off + done > ext2.size(v, ino) {
        ext2.set_size(v, ino, off + done)
    }
    touch_change(i)
    done
}

/// `ftruncate` on a volume.
fn vtruncate(i: u64, size: u64) -> u64 {
    let v = vol(i)
    if ext2.read_only(v) != 0 {
        return neg(EROFS)
    }
    if size > ext2.max_size(v) {
        return neg(EFBIG)
    }
    if size < ext2.size(v, vino(i)) {
        cut(i, size)
        let r = ext2.truncate(v, vino(i), size)
        if r != 0 {
            return r
        }
    } else {
        ext2.set_size(v, vino(i), size)
    }
    touch_change(i)
    0
}

fn vset_nlink(i: u64, n: u64) {
    ext2.set_nlink(vol(i), vino(i), n)
    ip(i, I_NLINK, n)
}

/// A volume inode's mode word written from the record's mirror, its
/// ctime moved.
fn vmode(i: u64) {
    if ext2.read_only(vol(i)) == 0 {
        ext2.set_mode(vol(i), vino(i), ig(i, I_MODE))
        ext2.touch(vol(i), vino(i), ext2.T_CTIME, now())
    }
}

/// A volume inode loses a name: its count down, its ctime moved, and
/// with no name and no holder left it goes.
fn vdrop_name(i: u64) {
    let n = ig(i, I_NLINK)
    vset_nlink(i, if n > 0 { n - 1 } else { 0 })
    ext2.touch(vol(i), vino(i), ext2.T_CTIME, now())
    if n <= 1 && ig(i, I_REFS) == 0 {
        vgone(i)
    }
}

/// A new inode of mode `m` named [name, name + len) in volume directory
/// `d`: `make`'s, on the disk.
fn vmake(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64, m: u64, uid: u64, gid: u64) -> u64 {
    let v = vol(d)
    if ext2.read_only(v) != 0 {
        return neg(EROFS)
    }
    if ig(d, I_NLINK) == 0 {
        return neg(ENOENT)
    }
    let t = now()
    let ino = ext2.ialloc(v, vino(d), m, uid, gid, t)
    if failed(ino) {
        return ino
    }
    ext2.set_nlink(v, ino, 1)
    let r = ext2.add(v, vino(d), name, len, ino, ext2.ftype(m))
    if failed(r) {
        ext2.set_nlink(v, ino, 0)
        ext2.ifree(v, ino, now_s())
        return r
    }
    ext2.touch(v, vino(d), ext2.T_MTIME | ext2.T_CTIME, t)
    let i = vrec(v, ino, d)
    if i == NONE {
        return neg(ENOMEM)
    }
    i
}

fn vmkdir(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64, perm: u64, uid: u64, gid: u64) -> u64 {
    let v = vol(d)
    if ext2.read_only(v) != 0 {
        return neg(EROFS)
    }
    if ig(d, I_NLINK) == 0 {
        return neg(ENOENT)
    }
    if ig(d, I_NLINK) >= ext2.LINK_MAX {
        return neg(EMLINK)
    }
    let t = now()
    let ino = ext2.ialloc(v, vino(d), S_IFDIR | (perm & 0xfff), uid, gid, t)
    if failed(ino) {
        return ino
    }
    let r = ext2.make_dir(v, ino, vino(d))
    if failed(r) {
        ext2.ifree(v, ino, now_s())
        return r
    }
    ext2.set_nlink(v, ino, 2)
    let r2 = ext2.add(v, vino(d), name, len, ino, 2)
    if failed(r2) {
        ext2.set_nlink(v, ino, 0)
        ext2.ifree(v, ino, now_s())
        return r2
    }
    vset_nlink(d, ig(d, I_NLINK) + 1)
    ext2.touch(v, vino(d), ext2.T_MTIME | ext2.T_CTIME, t)
    let i = vrec(v, ino, d)
    if i == NONE {
        return neg(ENOMEM)
    }
    i
}

fn vsymlink(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64, target: u64, tlen: u64, uid: u64, gid: u64) -> u64 {
    let v = vol(d)
    if ext2.read_only(v) != 0 {
        return neg(EROFS)
    }
    if ig(d, I_NLINK) == 0 {
        return neg(ENOENT)
    }
    let t = now()
    let ino = ext2.ialloc(v, vino(d), S_IFLNK | 0x1ff, uid, gid, t)
    if failed(ino) {
        return ino
    }
    let r = ext2.set_target(v, ino, target, tlen)
    if failed(r) {
        ext2.ifree(v, ino, now_s())
        return r
    }
    ext2.set_nlink(v, ino, 1)
    let r2 = ext2.add(v, vino(d), name, len, ino, 7)
    if failed(r2) {
        ext2.set_nlink(v, ino, 0)
        ext2.ifree(v, ino, now_s())
        return r2
    }
    ext2.touch(v, vino(d), ext2.T_MTIME | ext2.T_CTIME, t)
    let i = vrec(v, ino, d)
    if i == NONE {
        return neg(ENOMEM)
    }
    i
}

fn vlink(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64, i: u64) -> u64 {
    let v = vol(d)
    if vol(i) != v {
        return neg(EXDEV)
    }
    if ext2.read_only(v) != 0 {
        return neg(EROFS)
    }
    if ig(d, I_NLINK) == 0 || ig(i, I_NLINK) == 0 {
        return neg(ENOENT)
    }
    if ig(i, I_NLINK) >= ext2.LINK_MAX {
        return neg(EMLINK)
    }
    let r = ext2.add(v, vino(d), name, len, vino(i), ext2.ftype(ig(i, I_MODE)))
    if failed(r) {
        return r
    }
    let t = now()
    vset_nlink(i, ig(i, I_NLINK) + 1)
    ext2.touch(v, vino(i), ext2.T_CTIME, t)
    ext2.touch(v, vino(d), ext2.T_MTIME | ext2.T_CTIME, t)
    0
}

fn vunlink(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64) -> u64 {
    let v = vol(d)
    let n = ext2.lookup(v, vino(d), name, len)
    if n == 0 {
        return neg(ENOENT)
    }
    if ext2.read_only(v) != 0 {
        return neg(EROFS)
    }
    let i = vrec(v, n, d)
    if i == NONE {
        return neg(EIO)
    }
    if is_dir(i) {
        return neg(EISDIR)
    }
    let _gone = ext2.remove(v, vino(d), name, len)
    touch_change(d)
    vdrop_name(i)
    put_st(S_UNLINKS, st(S_UNLINKS) + 1)
    0
}

fn vrmdir(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64) -> u64 {
    let v = vol(d)
    let n = ext2.lookup(v, vino(d), name, len)
    if n == 0 {
        return neg(ENOENT)
    }
    if ext2.read_only(v) != 0 {
        return neg(EROFS)
    }
    let i = vrec(v, n, d)
    if i == NONE {
        return neg(EIO)
    }
    if !is_dir(i) {
        return neg(ENOTDIR)
    }
    if is_point(i) {
        return neg(EBUSY) // px67: a mount covers it
    }
    if !ext2.empty(v, n) {
        return neg(ENOTEMPTY)
    }
    let _gone = ext2.remove(v, vino(d), name, len)
    vset_nlink(d, if ig(d, I_NLINK) > 0 { ig(d, I_NLINK) - 1 } else { 0 })
    touch_change(d)
    vset_nlink(i, 0)
    ext2.touch(v, n, ext2.T_CTIME, now())
    if ig(i, I_REFS) == 0 {
        vgone(i)
    }
    0
}

fn vrename(od: u64, on: u64, ol: u64, nd: u64, nn: u64, nl: u64) -> u64 {
    let v = vol(od)
    if ig(nd, I_NLINK) == 0 {
        return neg(ENOENT)
    }
    let n = ext2.lookup(v, vino(od), on, ol)
    if n == 0 {
        return neg(ENOENT)
    }
    if ext2.read_only(v) != 0 {
        return neg(EROFS)
    }
    let i = vrec(v, n, od)
    if i == NONE {
        return neg(EIO)
    }
    let dir = is_dir(i)
    if is_point(i) {
        return neg(EBUSY) // px67: a mount covers it
    }
    if dir && below(nd, i) {
        return neg(EINVAL)
    }
    let ft = ext2.ftype(ig(i, I_MODE))
    let tn = ext2.lookup(v, vino(nd), nn, nl)
    if tn != 0 {
        let j = vrec(v, tn, nd)
        if j == NONE {
            return neg(EIO)
        }
        if j == i {
            return 0
        }
        if is_point(j) {
            return neg(EBUSY) // px67
        }
        if dir && !is_dir(j) {
            return neg(ENOTDIR)
        }
        if !dir && is_dir(j) {
            return neg(EISDIR)
        }
        if dir && !ext2.empty(v, tn) {
            return neg(ENOTEMPTY)
        }
        let _ok = ext2.relink(v, vino(nd), nn, nl, n, ft)
        let _gone = ext2.remove(v, vino(od), on, ol)
        if is_dir(j) {
            vset_nlink(nd, if ig(nd, I_NLINK) > 0 { ig(nd, I_NLINK) - 1 } else { 0 })
            vset_nlink(j, 0)
            ext2.touch(v, tn, ext2.T_CTIME, now())
            if ig(j, I_REFS) == 0 {
                vgone(j)
            }
        } else {
            vdrop_name(j)
        }
    } else {
        if dir && od != nd && ig(nd, I_NLINK) >= ext2.LINK_MAX {
            return neg(EMLINK)
        }
        let r = ext2.add(v, vino(nd), nn, nl, n, ft)
        if failed(r) {
            return r
        }
        let _gone = ext2.remove(v, vino(od), on, ol)
    }
    if dir && od != nd {
        ext2.set_dotdot(v, n, vino(nd))
        vset_nlink(od, if ig(od, I_NLINK) > 0 { ig(od, I_NLINK) - 1 } else { 0 })
        vset_nlink(nd, ig(nd, I_NLINK) + 1)
        hold(nd)
        let old = ig(i, I_PARENT)
        ip(i, I_PARENT, nd)
        release(old)
    }
    touch_change(od)
    touch_change(nd)
    ext2.touch(v, n, ext2.T_CTIME, now())
    0
}

/// px63: the entry of directory `d` at or after position `pos`, for
/// `getdents64`: (d_ino, 0 at the end; d_type; the name's kernel address;
/// its length; the position after it). A volume's directory answers its
/// own entries (`.` and `..` left to the caller) and their type bytes; the
/// memory's, its records.
pub fn dirent(d: u64, pos: u64) -> (u64, u64, u64, u64, u64) {
    if on_volume(d) {
        let (n, ft, a, l, nx) = ext2.entry_at(vol(d), vino(d), pos)
        return (n, dt_of(ft), a, l, nx)
    }
    let (i, a, l, nx) = entry_at(d, pos)
    if i == NONE {
        return (0, 0, 0, 0, nx)
    }
    let t = ig(i, I_MODE) & S_IFMT
    let dt = if t == S_IFDIR { 4 } else if t == S_IFLNK { 10 } else if t == S_IFSOCK { 12 } else if t == S_IFIFO { 1 } else { 8 }
    (i + 2, dt, a, l, nx)
}

/// A directory entry's type byte as `getdents64`'s d_type (directory.rst
/// and the uapi dirent's DT_*): regular 8, directory 4, character 2,
/// block 6, FIFO 1, socket 12, link 10, unknown 0.
fn dt_of(ft: u64) -> u64 {
    if ft == 1 { 8 } else if ft == 2 { 4 } else if ft == 3 { 2 } else if ft == 4 { 6 } else if ft == 5 { 1 } else if ft == 6 { 12 } else if ft == 7 { 10 } else { 0 }
}

/// px67: the record `/` is: the root mount's root when `/` is on a
/// volume (`root=`, kernel/fstab's `mount_root`), else the memory's ROOT.
/// kernel/files starts every absolute path here.
pub fn top() -> u64 {
    let r = st(S_ROOTM)
    if r == 0 { ROOT } else { mw(r - 1, M_ROOT) }
}

/// px67: whether `/` is on a volume.
pub fn root_on_volume() -> bool {
    st(S_ROOTM) != 0
}

/// px67: the mount whose root record `i` is (a volume's root, or the
/// memory's directory a memory mount puts over a volume's), or MOUNTS.
fn root_of(i: u64) -> u64 {
    if st(S_VOLF) == 0 {
        return MOUNTS
    }
    var k: u64 = 0
    while k < MOUNTS {
        if mw(k, M_POINT) != 0 && mw(k, M_ROOT) == i {
            return k
        }
        k += 1
    }
    MOUNTS
}

/// px67: whether record `i` is a mount's root (kernel/files: removing or
/// renaming it is -EBUSY).
pub fn is_mount_root(i: u64) -> bool {
    root_of(i) != MOUNTS
}

/// px67: the mount record `i` is the root of, or NONE.
pub fn mount_of_root(i: u64) -> u64 {
    let m = root_of(i)
    if m == MOUNTS { NONE } else { m }
}

fn free_mount() -> u64 {
    var k: u64 = 0
    while k < MOUNTS {
        if mw(k, M_POINT) == 0 {
            return k
        }
        k += 1
    }
    MOUNTS
}

/// The record standing for volume `v`'s root, made for its mount.
fn vroot_new(v: u64) -> u64 {
    let md = ext2.mode(v, ext2.ROOT_INO)
    let (u, g) = ext2.owner(v, ext2.ROOT_INO)
    let r = inode_new(md, u, g)
    if r == NONE {
        return NONE
    }
    put_st(S_LIVE, st(S_LIVE) - 1)
    put_st(S_VLIVE, st(S_VLIVE) + 1)
    let b = bucket(v, ext2.ROOT_INO)
    ip(r, I_NLINK, ext2.nlink(v, ext2.ROOT_INO))
    put_side(r, ext2.ROOT_INO | ((v + 1) << SD_VOL_SHIFT) | (rd(b) << SD_NEXT_SHIFT))
    wr(b, r + 1)
    r
}

/// Mount `m` takes root record `r` over directory `point`: the point is
/// held and marked, the root held by the mount (px63's rule), the order
/// it came in kept (px67).
fn attach(m: u64, point: u64, r: u64, v: u64, dev: u64, how: u64) -> u64 {
    ip(r, I_PARENT, point)
    hold(r) // the mount's
    hold(point)
    put_side(point, side(point) | SD_POINT | (m << SD_MOUNT_SHIFT))
    put_mw(m, M_POINT, point + 1)
    put_mw(m, M_ROOT, r)
    put_mw(m, M_VOL, v)
    put_mw(m, M_DEV, dev)
    put_vf(VF_SEQ, vf(VF_SEQ) + 1)
    put_mw(m, M_SEQ, vf(VF_SEQ))
    put_mw(m, M_HOW, how)
    put_mw(m, M_MODE, 0)
    m
}

/// Whether directory `point` may be covered: a directory, not covered
/// already, not a mount's root itself (px67: no mount is stacked on
/// another's root), and the volumes' frame there: 0 or -errno.
fn coverable(point: u64) -> u64 {
    if !is_dir(point) {
        return neg(ENOTDIR)
    }
    if !vol_ready() {
        return neg(ENOMEM)
    }
    if point == ROOT || is_point(point) || is_mount_root(point) {
        return neg(EBUSY)
    }
    0
}

/// px63: mount kernel/ext2's volume on disk `dev` at directory `point`
/// (px67: the memory's or a volume's, not `/`, not covered already, not
/// a mount's root), read-only when `ro`, written through when `how` has
/// MH_SYNC: its mount's number, or -errno (-ENOTDIR, -EBUSY, -ENOMEM,
/// ext2's own).
pub fn mount(point: u64, dev: u64, ro: bool, how: u64) -> u64 {
    let c = coverable(point)
    if c != 0 {
        return c
    }
    let m = free_mount()
    if m == MOUNTS {
        return neg(EBUSY)
    }
    let v = ext2.mount(dev, ro, now_s())
    if failed(v) {
        return v
    }
    let r = vroot_new(v)
    if r == NONE {
        let _u = ext2.unmount(v, now_s())
        return neg(ENOMEM)
    }
    attach(m, point, r, v, dev, how)
}

/// px67: `/` on volume `dev` (kernel/fstab's `root=`, before the first
/// program): the volume's root covers the memory's ROOT, and every path
/// starts there from now on (`top`). Once, at boot: -EBUSY after.
pub fn mount_root(dev: u64, ro: bool, how: u64) -> u64 {
    if st(S_ROOTM) != 0 || !ready() {
        return neg(EBUSY)
    }
    if !vol_ready() {
        return neg(ENOMEM)
    }
    let m = free_mount()
    if m == MOUNTS {
        return neg(EBUSY)
    }
    let v = ext2.mount(dev, ro, now_s())
    if failed(v) {
        return v
    }
    let r = vroot_new(v)
    if r == NONE {
        let _u = ext2.unmount(v, now_s())
        return neg(ENOMEM)
    }
    let k = attach(m, ROOT, r, v, dev, how | MH_ROOT)
    put_st(S_ROOTM, k + 1)
    k
}

/// px67 (R-px67-1): a directory of the memory's mounted over directory
/// `point` of a volume (`/tmp`, as a distribution's tmpfs), mode `perm`,
/// root's: its mount's number, or -errno. Its files are the memory's:
/// gone at the next boot.
pub fn mount_mem(point: u64, perm: u64) -> u64 {
    let c = coverable(point)
    if c != 0 {
        return c
    }
    let m = free_mount()
    if m == MOUNTS {
        return neg(EBUSY)
    }
    let r = inode_new(S_IFDIR | (perm & 0xfff), 0, 0)
    if r == NONE {
        return neg(ENOMEM)
    }
    ip(r, I_NLINK, 2)
    attach(m, point, r, NONE, NONE, 0)
}

/// px63: mount `m`'s volume (kernel/ext2's number), or NONE when the
/// mount is free or (px67) the memory's.
pub fn mounted(m: u64) -> u64 {
    if st(S_VOLF) == 0 || m >= MOUNTS || mw(m, M_POINT) == 0 { NONE } else { mw(m, M_VOL) }
}

/// px67: whether mount `m` is in use (a volume's or the memory's).
pub fn in_use(m: u64) -> bool {
    st(S_VOLF) != 0 && m < MOUNTS && mw(m, M_POINT) != 0
}

/// px63: mount `m`'s covered directory.
pub fn mount_point(m: u64) -> u64 {
    mw(m, M_POINT) - 1
}

/// px67: mount `m`'s root record, its disk (NONE for the memory's), its
/// order and what it was asked (MH_*).
pub fn mount_root_rec(m: u64) -> u64 {
    mw(m, M_ROOT)
}

pub fn mount_dev(m: u64) -> u64 {
    mw(m, M_DEV)
}

pub fn mount_seq(m: u64) -> u64 {
    mw(m, M_SEQ)
}

pub fn mount_how(m: u64) -> u64 {
    mw(m, M_HOW)
}

/// px67: what mount `m`'s line says it was asked (MH_*), kernel/fstab's
/// `/` and `tmpfs` lines and mount(2) setting it after the mount.
pub fn set_how(m: u64, how: u64) {
    if in_use(m) {
        put_mw(m, M_HOW, how | (mw(m, M_HOW) & MH_ROOT))
    }
}

/// px67: a memory mount's mode as asked, and the one it was given.
pub fn set_mode_of(m: u64, mode: u64) {
    if in_use(m) {
        put_mw(m, M_MODE, mode)
    }
}

pub fn mode_of(m: u64) -> u64 {
    mw(m, M_MODE)
}

/// px67: whether `/` (`top`) has a directory named `name`: the disk's
/// /dev, /proc and /sys the kernel's own trees are mounted over.
pub fn top_has(name: str) -> bool {
    let pa = frames.alloc() else 0
    if pa == 0 {
        return false
    }
    let b = pa + hh()
    var n: u64 = 0
    for c in name.bytes() {
        if n < 64 {
            // # Safety: a byte of the frame just taken, through the HHDM.
            unsafe { ((b + n) as *u8).write_volatile((c as int) as u8) }
        }
        n += 1
    }
    let c = lookup(top(), b, n)
    frames.free(pa)
    c != NONE && is_dir(c)
}

/// px67: whether mount `m` is `/`'s.
pub fn is_root_mount(m: u64) -> bool {
    st(S_ROOTM) == m + 1
}

/// px67: the mount in use with the least order above `after` (0: the
/// first), or MOUNTS: /proc/self/mounts' lines in the order they came.
pub fn mount_after(after: u64) -> u64 {
    var best = MOUNTS
    var k: u64 = 0
    while k < MOUNTS {
        if in_use(k) && mw(k, M_SEQ) > after && (best == MOUNTS || mw(k, M_SEQ) < mw(best, M_SEQ)) {
            best = k
        }
        k += 1
    }
    best
}

/// px67: let go of every record of volume `v` nobody holds, again and
/// again (a directory's record holds its parent's), but its root `r`:
/// whether any other is left (something holds it: an open file, a
/// working directory, a program running from it, a mount on it).
fn shed(v: u64, r: u64) -> bool {
    var more = true
    var guard: u64 = 0
    while more && guard < 64 {
        more = false
        var i: u64 = 0
        while i < st(S_NEXT) {
            let sd = side(i)
            if i != r && (sd >> SD_VOL_SHIFT) & 0xf == v + 1 && ig(i, I_MODE) != 0 && ig(i, I_REFS) == 0 && sd & SD_POINT == 0 {
                vdrop(i)
                more = true
            }
            i += 1
        }
        guard += 1
    }
    var i: u64 = 0
    while i < st(S_NEXT) {
        if i != r && (side(i) >> SD_VOL_SHIFT) & 0xf == v + 1 && ig(i, I_MODE) != 0 {
            return true
        }
        i += 1
    }
    false
}

/// px67: `umount2(2)` of mount `m` (not `/`'s: kernel/files remounts it
/// read-only instead, as Linux answers): -EBUSY while anything of it is
/// held (beyond the mount's own hold of its root) or, for the memory's,
/// while its directory has an entry; else the volume written, marked
/// clean when it was clean at the mount, and let go: 0 or -EIO.
pub fn unmount(m: u64) -> u64 {
    if !in_use(m) {
        return neg(EINVAL)
    }
    if is_root_mount(m) {
        return neg(EBUSY)
    }
    let r = mw(m, M_ROOT)
    let point = mw(m, M_POINT) - 1
    let v = mw(m, M_VOL)
    var e: u64 = 0
    if v == NONE {
        if ig(r, I_REFS) > 1 || ig(r, I_ENTRIES) != 0 {
            return neg(EBUSY)
        }
        ip(r, I_REFS, 0)
        ip(r, I_NLINK, 0)
        ip(r, I_PARENT, r) // the point is let go below, once
        put_mw(m, M_POINT, 0)
        inode_free(r)
    } else {
        if shed(v, r) || ig(r, I_REFS) > 1 {
            return neg(EBUSY)
        }
        writeback(r)
        cut(r, 0)
        e = ext2.unmount(v, now_s())
        unhash(r)
        put_side(r, 0)
        ip(r, I_MODE, 0)
        ip(r, I_REFS, 0)
        ip(r, I_NEXT, st(S_FREE))
        put_st(S_FREE, r + 1)
        put_st(S_VLIVE, st(S_VLIVE) - 1)
        put_mw(m, M_POINT, 0)
    }
    put_side(point, side(point) & !(SD_POINT | (7 << SD_MOUNT_SHIFT)))
    release(point)
    e
}

/// px67: `mount(2)`'s MS_REMOUNT of mount `m`'s volume, read-only when
/// `ro` (kernel/files refuses it -EBUSY first while a file of it is open
/// for writing, as Linux does): every shared page written, then
/// kernel/ext2's `remount`. 0 or -errno; -EINVAL for the memory's.
pub fn remount(m: u64, ro: bool) -> u64 {
    if !in_use(m) {
        return neg(EINVAL)
    }
    let v = mw(m, M_VOL)
    if v == NONE {
        return if ro { neg(EINVAL) } else { 0 }
    }
    writeback_vol(v)
    ext2.remount(v, ro, now_s())
}

fn writeback_vol(v: u64) {
    var i: u64 = 0
    while i < st(S_NEXT) {
        let s = side(i)
        if s & SD_SHARED != 0 && (s >> SD_VOL_SHIFT) & 0xf == v + 1 && ig(i, I_MODE) != 0 {
            writeback(i)
        }
        i += 1
    }
}

/// px63: `sync(2)`: every mounted volume's shared pages and dirty blocks
/// written and its disk flushed: 0 or the first -EIO.
pub fn sync_all() -> u64 {
    var err: u64 = 0
    var m: u64 = 0
    while m < MOUNTS {
        let v = mounted(m)
        if v != NONE {
            writeback_vol(v)
            let r = ext2.sync(v)
            if r != 0 && err == 0 {
                err = r
            }
        }
        m += 1
    }
    err
}

/// px63: `fsync(2)` and `syncfs(2)` of inode `i`: its volume's dirty
/// blocks written (the file's shared pages first) and the disk flushed;
/// 0 for the memory (nothing to write) or -EIO.
pub fn sync_of(i: u64) -> u64 {
    if !on_volume(i) {
        return 0
    }
    writeback(i)
    ext2.sync(vol(i))
}

/// px63: the end (a halt, a reboot): every volume's shared pages and
/// dirty blocks written, marked clean, flushed and let go: 0 or the
/// first -EIO. The records stay: nothing runs after. px67: in the
/// reverse of the order they were mounted, `/` last (the root's is the
/// first mount): each written, then marked clean, then flushed, as a
/// remount read-only would leave it, so a volume another is mounted on
/// is let go after it.
pub fn halt_volumes() -> u64 {
    var err: u64 = 0
    var guard: u64 = 0
    while guard <= MOUNTS {
        var last = MOUNTS
        var k: u64 = 0
        while k < MOUNTS {
            if in_use(k) && (last == MOUNTS || mw(k, M_SEQ) > mw(last, M_SEQ)) {
                last = k
            }
            k += 1
        }
        if last == MOUNTS {
            break
        }
        let v = mw(last, M_VOL)
        if v != NONE {
            writeback_vol(v)
            // PLANT px67-plant-clean: `/` written back, its clean flag skipped.
            let r = if is_root_mount(last) { 0 } else { ext2.unmount(v, now_s()) }
            if r != 0 && err == 0 {
                err = r
            }
        }
        put_mw(last, M_POINT, 0)
        guard += 1
    }
    err
}

/// px67: the regular file at the absolute path `path` (from `/`, `top`:
/// on the disk when `/` is; through mounts, no link followed) read whole
/// into a frame of its own, for the tables the kernel reads before the
/// first program (kmain_console's /etc/pax-run, kernel/fstab's
/// /etc/fstab): (its kernel address, its length, 0); the third word says
/// why there is none: 1 no such regular file, 2 longer than a page (the
/// length then its size), 3 no frame. The frame is never given back.
pub fn small_file(path: str) -> (u64, u64, u64) {
    let pa = frames.alloc() else 0
    if pa == 0 {
        return (0, 0, 3)
    }
    let b = pa + hh()
    var n: u64 = 0
    for c in path.bytes() {
        if n < PAGE {
            // # Safety: a byte of the frame just taken, through the HHDM.
            unsafe { ((b + n) as *u8).write_volatile((c as int) as u8) }
        }
        n += 1
    }
    var d = top()
    var i: u64 = 0
    var f = NONE
    var gone = false
    while i < n && !gone {
        while i < n && rd8(b + i) == 47 {
            i += 1
        }
        if i >= n {
            break
        }
        let s0 = i
        while i < n && rd8(b + i) != 47 {
            i += 1
        }
        if !is_dir(d) {
            gone = true
        } else {
            let c = lookup(d, b + s0, i - s0)
            if c == NONE {
                gone = true
            } else {
                f = c
                d = c
            }
        }
    }
    if gone || f == NONE || !is_regular(f) {
        frames.free(pa)
        return (0, 0, 1)
    }
    let sz = bytes(f)
    if sz > PAGE {
        frames.free(pa)
        return (0, sz, 2)
    }
    read_page(f, 0, b)
    (b, sz, 0)
}

/// px63: `statfs`'s field `w` (kernel/ext2's `statfs` numbering) for the
/// volume inode `i` is on.
pub fn vol_statfs(i: u64, w: u64) -> u64 {
    if !on_volume(i) {
        return 0
    }
    ext2.statfs(vol(i), w)
}

/// px63: records standing for a volume's inodes (0), given back while
/// their inode lives (1), frames the side table and the hash hold (2).
pub fn vol_books(which: u64) -> u64 {
    if which == 0 {
        return st(S_VLIVE)
    }
    if which == 1 {
        return st(S_VEVICT)
    }
    st(S_VSIDE)
}

// --- the tree made ------------------------------------------------------------------

/// The root directory's inode.
pub const ROOT: u64 = 0

fn make_dir(d: u64, name: u64, len: u64, perm: u64, uid: u64, gid: u64) -> u64 {
    let i = mkdir(d, name, len, perm, uid, gid)
    if failed(i) {
        panic.fail("tree: no room for a directory of the initramfs, frames held", st(S_HELD))
    }
    i
}

/// Archive entry `e` becomes an inode under the root: every directory
/// on its path made when missing (0755, root's), then the entry itself
/// — a directory with its mode, a file whose bytes are the archive's
/// own, or (px64) a symbolic link whose target is the entry's data (1
/// to 4095 bytes, as `symlink(2)` takes; another length is left out) —
/// owned as the archive says (px42: the header's uid and gid; pax#48).
/// Anything else (a device, a FIFO) is left out.
fn adopt(e: u64) {
    let a = initramfs.name_addr(e)
    let l = initramfs.name_length(e)
    let m = initramfs.mode(e)
    let t = initramfs.mtime(e) * NS_PER_SEC
    let eu = initramfs.uid(e)
    let eg = initramfs.gid(e)
    put_st(S_STAMP, t + 1)
    var d = ROOT
    var s: u64 = 0
    while s < l {
        var k = s
        while k < l && rd8(a + k) != 47 {
            k += 1
        }
        let n = k - s
        var last = true
        var j = k
        while j < l {
            if rd8(a + j) != 47 {
                last = false
            }
            j += 1
        }
        if n == 0 || n > NAME_MAX || (n == 1 && rd8(a + s) == 46) {
            s = k + 1
            continue
        }
        let c = lookup(d, a + s, n)
        if !last {
            if c == NONE {
                d = make_dir(d, a + s, n, 0x1ed, 0, 0)
            } else if is_dir(c) {
                d = c
            } else {
                return
            }
        } else if m & S_IFMT == S_IFDIR {
            let i = if c == NONE { make_dir(d, a + s, n, m & 0xfff, eu, eg) } else { c }
            if is_dir(i) {
                ip(i, I_MODE, S_IFDIR | (m & 0xfff))
                ip(i, I_OWNER, pack(eu, eg))
                ip(i, I_ATIME, t)
                ip(i, I_MTIME, t)
                ip(i, I_CTIME, t)
                ip(i, I_BTIME, t)
            }
        } else if m & S_IFMT == S_IFREG && c == NONE {
            let i = create(d, a + s, n, m & 0xfff, eu, eg)
            if failed(i) {
                panic.fail("tree: no room for a file of the initramfs, frames held", st(S_HELD))
            }
            let size = initramfs.size(e)
            ip(i, I_SIZE, size)
            ip(i, I_BACK, initramfs.data(e))
            ip(i, I_BACKLEN, size)
            ip(i, I_ENTRIES, e + 1)
        } else if m & S_IFMT == S_IFLNK && c == NONE {
            let size = initramfs.size(e)
            if size >= 1 && size < PAGE {
                let i = symlink(d, a + s, n, initramfs.data(e), size, eu, eg)
                if failed(i) {
                    panic.fail("tree: no room for a link of the initramfs, frames held", st(S_HELD))
                }
            }
        }
        s = k + 1
    }
}

/// Make the tree (once, at boot, before the first program: kernel/user's
/// `start`): the cap, the inode table, the page of zeros, the root, and
/// an inode for every entry of the initramfs when there is one.
pub fn start() {
    if st(S_READY) != 0 {
        return
    }
    put_st(S_CAP, frames.free_count() / 2)
    let t = grab()
    let z = grab()
    if t == 0 || z == 0 {
        panic.fail("tree: no frame for the inode table, frames free", frames.free_count())
    }
    put_st(S_TABLE, t)
    put_st(S_ZERO, z)
    put_st(S_STAMP, 1)
    let r = inode_new(S_IFDIR | 0x1ed, 0, 0)
    if r != ROOT {
        panic.fail("tree: the root is not inode 0 but", r)
    }
    ip(r, I_PARENT, r)
    ip(r, I_NLINK, 2)
    put_st(S_READY, 1)
    if initramfs.bytes() != 0 && initramfs.problem() == 0 {
        var e = initramfs.first() else initramfs.END
        while e != initramfs.END {
            adopt(e)
            e = initramfs.next(e) else initramfs.END
        }
    }
    put_st(S_STAMP, 0)
    put_st(S_BASE, st(S_HELD))
    put_st(S_BASE_LIVE, st(S_LIVE))
    put_st(S_BASE_ITABLE, st(S_ITABLE))
}

/// Whether `start` has run.
pub fn ready() -> bool {
    st(S_READY) != 0
}
